symptoms and complications.DYSFUNCTION:Dysfunction refers to impaired or abnormal functioning, which can occur in various systems of the body in patients with mitochondrial diseases like MELAS syndrome.MITOCHONDRIAL DISORDERS:MAR√çA JOS√â MOLINA PUERTA:Mar√≠a Jos√© Molina Puerta is a specialist in Endocrinology and Nutrition at Hospital Universitario Reina Sof√≠a in C√≥rdoba.HOSPITAL UNIVERSITARIO REINA SOF√çA:Hospital Universitario Reina Sof√≠a is a medical institution located in C√≥rdoba, specializing in various healthcare services.BYPASS G√ÅSTRICO:Gastric bypass is a type of weight-loss surgery that involves creating a small pouch from the stomach and connecting it directly to the small intestine.DEHISCENCIA DE SUTURA:Suture dehiscence is a complication that occurs when a surgical wound reopens, which can happen postoperatively.NUTRICI√ìN ENTERAL TOTAL:NUTRICI√ìN ENTERAL TOTAL, also known as total enteral nutrition, is a method of feeding that delivers all nutritional requirements directly through the gastrointestinal tract. This approach was specifically implemented for a patient following bariatric surgery due to complications that arose during the recovery process.NUTRICI√ìN PARENTERAL TOTAL:NUTRICI√ìN PARENTERAL TOTAL, also known as Total Parenteral Nutrition (TPN), is a treatment designed to deliver nutrients directly into the bloodstream, bypassing the gastrointestinal tract. This method is particularly utilized for patients who are unable to consume food orally. In the case of a specific patient, TPN was initiated following the loss of a nasoenteric tube and prior to the resumption of oral feeding. During the patient's hospitalization, TPN served as a crucial means of providing nutritional support, ensuring that the necessary nutrients were supplied directly into the bloodstream to meet the patient's dietary needs.MUJER DE 48 A√ëOS:Una mujer de 48 a√±os que ha sido intervenida de cirug√≠a bari√°trica y tiene antecedentes de diabetes tipo 2 y obesidad m√≥rbida.ENDOCOPIA DIGESTIVA ALTA:Procedimiento m√©dico que fue muy mal tolerado por la paciente durante la evaluaci√≥n de su condici√≥n.MEDICAMENTOS:Tratamientos habituales de la paciente que incluyen metformina, liraglutida, insulina, losart√°n, atorvastatina, ezetrol y adiro.HIPERLIPEMIA:Condici√≥n m√©dica de la paciente que se menciona como parte de sus antecedentes personales.S√çNDROME DEPRESIVO:Condici√≥n m√©dica de la paciente que se menciona como parte de sus antecedentes personales.S√çNDROME DE APNEA OBSTRUCTIVA DEL SUE√ëO:Condici√≥n m√©dica de la paciente que est√° pendiente de confirmaci√≥n mediante estudio.MEFORMINA:Medicamento utilizado por la paciente para el control de la diabetes tipo 2.LIRAGLUTIDE:Medicamento utilizado por la paciente, administrado como inyecci√≥n para el control de la diabetes tipo 2.LOSART√ÅN:Medicamento utilizado por la paciente para el tratamiento de la hipertensi√≥n arterial.ATORVASTATINA:Atorvastatin is a medication that the patient takes to manage dyslipidemia and lower cholesterol levels. It is utilized by the patient for the control of blood lipids, indicating its role in maintaining healthy cholesterol levels and overall cardiovascular health.EZETROL:Medicamento utilizado por la paciente para el control de l√≠pidos en sangre.ADIRO:Medicamento utilizado por la paciente como parte de su tratamiento habitual.HIIPERTENSI√ìN ARTERIAL:ENDOSCOPIA DIGESTIVA ALTA:La endoscopia digestiva alta es un procedimiento realizado para evaluar el estado del es√≥fago, est√≥mago y duodeno de la paciente, que mostr√≥ una hernia de hiato y mucosa normal.ENFERMER√çA EDUCADORA:La enfermera educadora es responsable de la educaci√≥n nutricional de la paciente antes de la cirug√≠a bari√°trica.TOMOGRAF√çA AXIAL COMPUTERIZADA:La tomograf√≠a axial computerizada fue realizada para confirmar la existencia de un trayecto fistuloso en la sutura gastroyeyunal tras la cirug√≠a.DIETA DIAB√âTICA HIPERPROTEICA:La dieta diab√©tica hiperproteica es el r√©gimen alimenticio que se implement√≥ para la paciente durante su recuperaci√≥n postoperatoria.F√çSTULA G√ÅSTRICA:La f√≠stula g√°strica es una complicaci√≥n postoperatoria que se sospech√≥ en la paciente tras la cirug√≠a bari√°trica.DRENAJE:El drenaje es un procedimiento que se realiz√≥ en la paciente para manejar el d√©bito sucio postoperatorio tras la cirug√≠a bari√°trica.FEDERACI√ìN INTERNACIONAL DE DIABETES:The Federaci√≥n Internacional de Diabetes (IDF) is an organization dedicated to establishing guidelines and recommendations for the treatment of diabetes. It plays a crucial role in providing guidance on various aspects of diabetes management, including the consideration of metabolic surgery for patients suffering from morbid obesity. Through its efforts, the IDF aims to improve the care and outcomes for individuals affected by diabetes worldwide.CONTROL GLUC√âMICO:Control gluc√©mico refers to the management and regulation of a patient's blood glucose levels throughout their treatment. It is a crucial aspect of patient care, particularly involving the administration of insulin to effectively manage blood glucose levels. In the context of treatment with NET (Nutritional Enteral Therapy) and NPT (Nutritional Parenteral Therapy), the control gluc√©mico was noted to be adequate, ensuring that the patient's glucose levels were maintained within a desirable range during their treatment.TRATAMIENTO M√âDICO INTENSIVO:El tratamiento m√©dico intensivo se refiere a las intervenciones m√©dicas que se aplican a la paciente para el control de la diabetes tipo 2, complementando la cirug√≠a bari√°trica.ESTUDIO STAMPEDE:El estudio STAMPEDE es una investigaci√≥n que demuestra la efectividad de la cirug√≠a bari√°trica en el control gluc√©mico en pacientes obesos con diabetes tipo 2.ASOCIACI√ìN AMERICANA DE DIABETES:The Asociaci√≥n Americana de Diabetes (ADA) provides recommendations for diabetes management, including the possibility of surgery for certain patients.SOCIEDAD ESPA√ëOLA PARA EL E