 means.FUGA ANASTOM√ìTICA:Fuga anastom√≥tica is a common complication after metabolic surgery that may require nutritional support due to its impact on oral intake.NA√öSEAS Y V√ìMITOS:Nauseas y v√≥mitos are common post-operative complications that can limit a patient's ability to eat normally after metabolic surgery.MALABSORCI√ìN SEVERA:Malabsorci√≥n severa is a serious condition that can occur post-surgery, affecting nutrient absorption and necessitating nutritional support.DIETA ORAL:Dieta oral refers to the normal diet that most patients transition to after metabolic surgery, although some may face complications that prevent this.CALORIMETR√çA INDIRECTA:Calorimetr√≠a indirecta is a method used to measure basal metabolic rate, which is important for determining nutritional needs in post-operative patients.EQUACIONES PREDICTIVAS:Ecuaciones predictivas are formulas used to estimate metabolic expenditure in patients, especially when calorimetry is unavailable.)<|COMPLETE|>SOCIEDAD AMERICANA DE NUTRICI√ìN PARENTERAL Y ENTERAL:ASPEN is an organization that provides guidelines for nutritional support in hospitalized adult obese patients, particularly in the context of bariatric surgery.NUTRICI√ìN HIPERPROTEICA:Hyperproteic nutrition is recommended for patients without severe liver or kidney dysfunction, aiming to avoid negative consequences of overfeeding.NUTRICI√ìN HIPOCAL√ìRICA:Hypocaloric nutrition is designed to prevent negative outcomes associated with overfeeding, such as hyperglycemia and increased infection rates.UNIDAD DE CUIDADOS INTENSIVOS:The Intensive Care Unit (UCI) is a specialized department in hospitals where patients receive close monitoring and care, particularly for nutritional adjustments.NIVEL DE RECOMENDACI√ìN BAJO:A low level of recommendation indicates that the evidence supporting a particular nutritional approach is not strong, as seen in the guidelines for nutritional support in bariatric surgery.NIVELES DE CUIDADO:Levels of care refer to the different intensities of medical care provided, particularly in the context of monitoring nutritional intake in critical patients.PAR√ÅMETROS CL√çNICOS:Clinical parameters are metrics used to assess a patient's health status, including wound healing and early mobilization in the context of nutritional support.DEFICIENCIAS NUTRICIONALES:Nutritional deficiencies are conditions that arise when the body does not get enough nutrients, which can be a risk for patients undergoing bariatric surgery.FLUIDOS Y ELECTROLITOS:Fluids and electrolytes are essential for maintaining hydration and electrolyte balance, which must be closely monitored in patients receiving nutritional support.NIVELES DE GLUCEMIA:Blood glucose levels are monitored to manage the metabolic state of patients, particularly those undergoing bariatric surgery.)<|COMPLETE|>HOSPITAL GENERAL UNIVERSITARIO MORALES MESEGUER:Hospital General Universitario Morales Meseguer is a healthcare institution located in Murcia, specializing in various medical fields including endocrinology and nutrition.YAMINA SULEIMAN MARTOS:Dra. Yamina Suleiman Martos is a specialist in endocrinology and nutrition, involved in the clinical management of diabetes and related conditions.MURCIA:Murcia is a region in Spain where the Hospital General Universitario Morales Meseguer is located.MNGIE:MNGIE, or mitochondrial neurogastrointestinal encephalomyopathy, is a rare genetic disorder characterized by a deficiency in thymidine phosphorylase, which is caused by mutations in the TYMP gene. This disorder primarily affects the gastrointestinal and nervous systems, resulting in a range of metabolic issues and complications, including diabetes. Due to the complexity of the symptoms and the interplay between the affected systems, MNGIE requires intricate treatment approaches to manage its severe manifestations.NUTRICIONAL SUPPLEMENTS:Nutritional supplements are products taken to enhance dietary intake, often used in clinical settings to support patients with specific health conditions.FENOFIBRATO:Fenofibrate is a medication used to reduce cholesterol levels and triglycerides in the blood, often prescribed for patients with metabolic disorders.OMEPRAZOL:Omeprazol is a medication that the patient is taking to reduce the production of acid in the stomach. It is commonly used to treat gastroesophageal reflux disease and other related conditions.SUPLEMENTOS VITAM√çNICOS:Vitamin supplements are dietary supplements that provide vitamins, often used to address deficiencies in patients with specific health conditions.BARIATRIC SURGERY:NEUROPAT√çA √ìPTICA BILATERAL:La neuropat√≠a √≥ptica bilateral es un diagn√≥stico que se presenta a los 10-12 a√±os, caracterizado por la disminuci√≥n progresiva de la agudeza visual y la atrofia √≥ptica observada en el fondo de ojo.POLINEUROPAT√çA SENSITIVO MOTORA AXONAL:La polineuropat√≠a sensitivo motora axonal es un diagn√≥stico que se presenta a los 16 a√±os, caracterizado por debilidad progresiva en miembros y amiotrofia distal.HIPOACUSIA PROFUNDA BILATERAL:La hipoacusia profunda bilateral neurosensorial es un diagn√≥stico que se presenta a los 30 a√±os, que requiere la colocaci√≥n de un implante coclear debido a la severidad de la p√©rdida auditiva.LEUCOENCEFALOPAT√çA SUPRATENTORIAL:La leucoencefalopat√≠a supratentorial periventricular difusa es un hallazgo observado en la resonancia magn√©tica nuclear cerebral, indicando cambios en la sustancia blanca del cerebro.S√çNTOMAS DIGESTIVOS:Los s√≠ntomas digestivos incluyen p√©rdida de peso, deposiciones blandas y episodios diarreicos, que se presentan en el paciente a lo largo del tiempo.AN√ÅLISIS DE SANGRE:The entity "AN√ÅLISIS DE SANGRE" refers to blood tests conducted on patients to assess various health indicators. These tests are essential for monitoring glucose levels, renal function, and other critical health parameters. The blood analysis reveals several important metrics, including blood sugar (glucemia), cholesterol levels, and vitamin concentrations, all of which are relevant for diagnosing the patient's health status. Overall, blood tests serve as a vital tool in evaluating the patient's overall health and nutritional parameters.ENDOSCOPIA:La endoscopia revela mucosa con atrofia parcheada y linfangiectasias, lo que contribuye al diagn√≥stico del paciente.C√ÅPSULA ENDOSC√ìPICA:La c√°psula endosc√≥pica visualiza linfangiectasias y edema en el yeyuno proximal, proporcionando informaci√≥n adicional sobre la condici√≥n del paciente.ATROFIA √ìPTICA:La atrofia √≥ptica es un hallazgo observado en el fondo de ojo del paciente, indicando da√±o severo en la v√≠a visual.DEBILIDAD PROGRESIVA:La debilidad progresiva es un s√≠ntoma que se presenta a los 16 a√±os, afectando principalmente a los miembros inferiores y superiores.HIPOGLICEMIAS:Las hipoglucemias son episodios que ocurren debido a la suspensi√≥n irregular del tratamiento antidiab√©tico, afectando la salud del paciente.SENSACI√ìN DE PLENITUD POSTPRANDIAL:La sensaci√≥n de plenitud postprandial es un s√≠ntoma que el paciente experimenta despu√©s de las comidas, indicando problemas digestivos.IMAGEN DE RMN:La imagen de resonancia magn√©tica nuclear (RMN) muestra cambios en la sustancia blanca del cerebro, lo que es relevante para el diagn√≥stico del paciente.MUCOSA INTESTINAL:La mucosa intestinal presenta atrofia y linfangiectasias, lo que se observa durante la endoscopia y es relevante para el diagn√≥stico del paciente.PATOLOG√çAS:TYMP:The TYMP gene is located on chromosome 22q13.33 and encodes a protein involved in the phosphorylation of thymidine, mutations in which cause MNGIE.GARONE:Garone is a researcher who reviewed 102 cases of MNGIE between 1988 and 2011, contributing to the understanding of the syndrome.TIMIDINA:Thymidine is a nucleoside that accumulates in patients with MNGIE due to the deficiency of thymidine phosphorylase.DEOXIURIDINA:Deoxyuridine is another nucleoside that accumulates in patients with MNGIE, indicating a metabolic disturbance.ALHAMIA PRISON:Alhamia Prison is a facility mentioned in the context of MNGIE, although not directly related to the syndrome itself.NEUROLOGICAL SYMPTOMS:Neurological symptoms associated with MNGIE include peripheral neuropathy, ptosis, ophthalmoplegia, and leukoencephalopathy.DIGESTIVE SYMPTOMS:Digestive symptoms of MNGIE include gastrointestinal dysmotility, early satiety, nausea, vomiting, and abdominal pain.CAQUEXIA:CAQUEXIA is a significant medical condition characterized by involuntary weight loss and muscle mass loss. It is particularly prevalent in patients suffering from Mitochondrial Neurogastrointestinal Encephalomyopathy (MNGIE), where it arises due to severe digestive symptoms. Additionally, cachexia is commonly observed in patients with advanced cancer, notably in those with adenocarcinoma of the pancreas. This condition not only contributes to malnutrition but also poses a considerable risk for further nutritional deficiencies. Overall, cachexia is a critical factor influencing the prognosis of affected individuals, especially in the context of cancer-related illnesses.ANALYTICAL FINDINGS:Analytical findings in MNGIE include elevated levels of thymidine and deoxyuridine in plasma, which are characteristic of the disorder.NEUROIMAGING FINDINGS:Neuroimaging findings in MNGIE typically show diffuse alterations in white matter, indicative of leukoencephalopathy.GENETIC SEQUENCING:Genetic sequencing is performed to identify mutations in the TYMP gene, confirming the diagnosis of MNGIE.CHROMOSOME 22Q13.33:COENZYME Q 10:Coenzyme Q 10 is an antioxidant and a vital component of the mitochondrial respiratory chain, evaluated for its effects in mitochondrial diseases.CREATINE:Creatine is a substance that has been studied for its potential benefits in improving muscle strength in patients with mitochondrial diseases.THYMIDINE PHOSPHORYLASE:Thymidine phosphorylase is an enzyme whose activity is crucial for the metabolism of thymidine, and its deficiency is linked to MNGIE.HEMATOPOIETIC STEM CELL TRANSPLANT:Hematopoietic stem cell transplant is a treatment option being explored to correct the enzymatic deficiency in MNGIE.DIETARY ANTIOXIDANTS:Dietary antioxidants, including idebenone and vitamin E, have been studied for their potential clinical benefits in mitochondrial diseases.ENFERMEDAD CEL√çACA:Enfermedad cel√≠aca is an autoimmune disorder that affects the gastrointestinal tract and is included in the differential diagnosis of mitochondrial diseases.S√çNDROME DE COLON IRRITABLE:S√≠ndrome de colon irritable is a gastrointestinal disorder that must be differentiated from mitochondrial diseases.DISTROFIA MUSCULAR CONG√âNITA:Distrofia muscular cong√©nita por d√©ficit de merosina is a genetic disorder that affects muscle function and is relevant in the differential diagnosis of mitochondrial diseases.LEUCODISTROFIAS:Leucodistrofias are a group of disorders affecting the white matter of the brain, included in the differential diagnosis of mitochondrial diseases.ENFERMEDAD DE KRABBE:Enfermedad de Krabbe is a type of leukodystrophy that must be differentiated from mitochondrial diseases.ADRENOLEUCODISTROFIA:Adrenoleucodistrofia is a genetic disorder affecting the adrenal glands and white matter of the brain, relevant in the differential diagnosis of mitochondrial diseases.ENFERMEDAD DE CANAVAN:Enfermedad de Canavan is a genetic disorder that affects the brain and is included in the differential diagnosis of mitochondrial diseases.ENFERMEDAD DE ALEXANDER:Enfermedad de Alexander is a type of leukodystrophy that must be differentiated from mitochondrial diseases.LEUCOENCEFALOPAT√çA CON SUSTANCIA BLANCA EVANESCENTE:Leucoencefalopat√≠a con sustancia blanca evanescente is a disorder affecting the brain's white matter, relevant in the differential diagnosis of mitochondrial diseases.POLINEUROPAT√çA DESMIELINIZANTE INFLAMATORIA CR√ìNICA:TIMIDIN FOSFORILASA:Thymidine phosphorylase is an enzyme whose activity is crucial for correcting metabolic damage in patients with MNGIE.HEPATITIS:Hepatic transplantation is considered a viable treatment option for MNGIE patients due to the liver's role in producing thymidine phosphorylase.DIABETES MITOCONDRIAL:Mitochondrial diabetes is a condition that complicates treatment in patients with MNGIE, requiring careful management of blood sugar levels.COENZIMA Q 10:Coenzyme Q10 is a supplement used in the treatment of mitochondrial disorders, including MNGIE, to support cellular energy production.L-CARNITINA:L-Carnitine is a supplement that may be beneficial in managing symptoms for patients with mitochondrial diseases, such as MNGIE. Additionally, it has the potential to increase body weight and enhance the quality of life for cancer patients.ANTIDIAB√âTICOS ORALES:Oral antidiabetic medications are prescribed to manage the patient's diabetes, which is complicated by mitochondrial dysfunction.SITAGLIPTINA:Sitagliptin is an oral antidiabetic medication utilized in the treatment regimen for patients with MNGIE (Mitochondrial Neurogastrointestinal Encephalomyopathy) as well as for controlling blood sugar levels in individuals with type 2 diabetes. This medication helps manage blood glucose levels effectively, making it a valuable option for patients requiring diabetes management.(N␀␀␀␀␀␀/O␀␀␀␀␀␀aS␀␀␀␀␀␀ T␀␀␀␀␀␀ºU␀␀␀␀␀␀úV␀␀␀␀␀␀nW␀␀␀␀␀␀ZX␀␀␀␀␀␀+Y␀␀␀␀␀␀Z␀␀␀␀␀␀Ω[␀␀␀␀␀␀ã\␀␀␀␀␀␀_]␀␀␀␀␀␀^␀␀␀␀␀␀h_␀␀␀␀␀␀…`␀␀␀␀␀␀2b␀␀␀␀␀␀!d␀␀␀␀␀␀“e␀␀␀␀␀␀h␀␀␀␀␀␀j␀␀␀␀␀␀Vk␀␀␀␀␀␀ìl␀␀␀␀␀␀Àm␀␀␀␀␀␀sp␀␀␀␀␀␀¬q␀␀␀␀␀␀.s␀␀␀␀␀␀]t␀␀␀␀␀␀Ùv␀␀␀␀␀␀Yx␀␀␀␀␀␀Öx␀␀␀␀␀␀ºx␀␀␀␀␀␀ z␀␀␀␀␀␀Õz␀␀␀␀␀␀P|␀␀␀␀␀␀⁄}␀␀␀␀␀␀Ω~␀␀␀␀␀␀}Ä␀␀␀␀␀␀3Å␀␀␀␀␀␀ŒÅ␀␀␀␀␀␀dÇ␀␀␀␀␀␀∏É␀␀␀␀␀␀ëÖ␀␀␀␀␀␀áá␀␀␀␀␀␀)à␀␀␀␀␀␀¥à␀␀␀␀␀␀*ä␀␀␀␀␀␀®ã␀␀␀␀␀␀§ç␀␀␀␀␀␀è␀␀␀␀␀␀eë␀␀␀␀␀␀í␀␀␀␀␀␀‡í␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ì␀␀␀␀␀␀ﬂì␀␀␀␀␀␀ï␀␀␀␀␀␀ó␀␀␀␀␀␀bò␀␀␀␀␀␀¸ò␀␀␀␀␀␀yô␀␀␀␀␀␀ö␀␀␀␀␀␀éö␀␀␀␀␀␀ù␀␀␀␀␀␀∆û␀␀␀␀␀␀°␀␀␀␀␀␀q¢␀␀␀␀␀␀jß␀␀␀␀␀␀0©␀␀␀␀␀␀≈´␀␀␀␀␀␀B¨␀␀␀␀␀␀␀≠␀␀␀␀␀␀Ÿ≠␀␀␀␀␀␀M¥␀␀␀␀␀␀ﬁ¥␀␀␀␀␀␀Üµ␀␀␀␀␀␀'∂␀␀␀␀␀␀ ∂␀␀␀␀␀␀Ç∑␀␀␀␀␀␀!∏␀␀␀␀␀␀∫∏␀␀␀␀␀␀√␀␀␀␀␀␀π√␀␀␀␀␀␀ƒ␀␀␀␀␀␀•∆␀␀␀␀␀␀\»␀␀␀␀␀␀iÀ␀␀␀␀␀␀)Ã