phasize the importance of nutrition in managing diabetes.\n\nThe company is represented by a logo featuring an orange four-leaf clover or flower-like symbol, which reflects its identity within the pharmaceutical industry. PERSAN FARMA is dedicated to enhancing the training of healthcare professionals in clinical nutrition through its scientific projects and publications. Additionally, it sponsors publications aimed at improving training in nutritional therapy for various pathologies related to diabetes mellitus, demonstrating its commitment to advancing knowledge and practices in this critical area of healthcare."}{"title": "HOSPITAL GENERAL UNIVERSITARIO DE ALICANTE:The Hospital General Universitario de Alicante is a healthcare institution that provides a range of medical services. Within this facility, Dr. \u00c1ngel Luis Abad Gonz\u00e1lez serves as a specialist in endocrinology and nutrition, contributing to the hospital's commitment to patient care and specialized medical treatment."}{"title": "HOSPITAL UNIVERSITARIO Y POLIT\u00c9CNICO DE LA FE, VALENCIA:Hospital Universitario y Polit\u00e9cnico de La Fe in Valencia is a healthcare institution where Dr. Juan Francisco Merino Torres works as a head of the endocrinology and nutrition service."}{"title": "HOSPITAL CL\u00cdNICO UNIVERSITARIO LOZANO BLESAS, ZARAGOZA:Hospital Cl\u00ednico Universitario Lozano Blesa in Zaragoza is a healthcare institution where Dr. Julia Oc\u00f3n Bret\u00f3n works as a specialist in endocrinology and nutrition."}{"title": "HOSPITAL UNIVERSITARIO SAN CECILIO, GRANADA:Hospital Universitario San Cecilio in Granada is a healthcare institution where Dr. Mar\u00eda Luisa Fern\u00e1ndez Soto works as a specialist in endocrinology and nutrition."}{"title": "HOSPITAL UNIVERSITARIO MARQU\u00c9S DE VALDECILLA, CANTABRIA:Hospital Universitario Marqu\u00e9s de Valdecilla in Cantabria is a healthcare institution where Dr. \u00c1ngela Gonz\u00e1lez D\u00edaz-Faes works as a specialist in endocrinology and nutrition."}{"title": "HOSPITAL UNIVERSITARIO 12 DE OCTUBRE, MADRID:Hospital Universitario 12 de Octubre in Madrid is a healthcare institution where Dr. Miguel Le\u00f3n Sanz works as the head of the endocrinology and nutrition service."}{"title": "HOSPITAL UNIVERSITARIO MIGUEL SERVET, ZARAGOZA:Hospital Universitario Miguel Servet in Zaragoza is a healthcare institution where Dr. Francisco Losfablos Callau works as a specialist in endocrinology and nutrition."}{"title": "HOSPITAL CL\u00cdNICO UNIVERSITARIO DE VALLADOLID:The Hospital Cl\u00ednico Universitario de Valladolid is a healthcare institution that serves as a medical facility in Valladolid. It is notable for having Dr. Daniel A. de Luis Rom\u00e1n as the head of its endocrinology and nutrition service. This institution is dedicated to providing comprehensive medical care and is recognized for its specialized services in the field of endocrinology and nutrition."}{"title": "HOSPITAL UNIVERSITARIO DE SAN JUAN, ALICANTE:Hospital Universitario de San Juan in Alicante is a healthcare institution where Dr. Rosa M\u00aa Mirete L\u00f3pez works as a specialist in endocrinology and nutrition."}{"title": "HOSPITAL UNIVERSITARIO REINA SOF\u00cdA, C\u00d3RDOBA:Hospital Universitario Reina Sof\u00eda in C\u00f3rdoba is a healthcare institution where Dr. Mar\u00eda Jos\u00e9 Molina Puerta works as a specialist in endocrinology and nutrition."}{"title": "HOSPITAL SAN PEDRO, LA RIOJA:Hospital San Pedro in La Rioja is a healthcare institution where Dr. \u00c1ngela Mart\u00edn Palmero works as the head of the clinical nutrition and dietetics unit."}{"title": "DRA. MAR\u00cdA ARGENTE PLA:Dra. Mar\u00eda Argente Pla is a medical specialist in endocrinology and nutrition at Hospital Universitario y Polit\u00e9cnico de La Fe in Valencia. She is known for her expertise in treating patients with diabetes mellitus and cystic fibrosis, providing specialized care to manage these chronic conditions effectively."}{"title": "DRA. MAR\u00cdA D. BALLESTEROS POMAR:Dra. Mar\u00eda D. Ballesteros Pomar is a medical specialist in endocrinology and nutrition, currently practicing at the Complejo Asistencial Universitario de Le\u00f3n. She is recognized for her expertise in the field and has contributed to the medical community through her authorship of articles related to diabetes mellitus."}{"title": "DR. FERNANDO L. CALVO GRACIA:Dr. Fernando L. Calvo Gracia is a medical specialist in Endocrinology and Nutrition at Hospital Cl\u00ednico Universitario Lozano Blesa in Zaragoza. He is particularly involved in managing nutritional support for patients with pancreatic tumors, demonstrating his expertise in both endocrinology and nutrition within a clinical setting."}{"title": "DRA. M\u00aa VICTORIA GARC\u00cdA ZAFRA:Dra. M\u00aa Victoria Garc\u00eda Zafra is a medical specialist in endocrinology and nutrition at Hospital General Universitario Santa Luc\u00eda in Cartagena. She is recognized for her work in providing nutritional support, particularly for patients with complex conditions such as MELAS syndrome and diabetes. As an author of one of the clinical cases presented, she emphasizes the importance of tailored nutritional interventions in managing these intricate health issues."}{"title": "DRA. MAR\u00cdA LUISA FERN\u00c1NDEZ SOTO:Dra. Mar\u00eda Luisa Fern\u00e1ndez Soto is a highly regarded specialist in Endocrinology and Nutrition. She serves as the scientific director and coordinator of the Clinical Nutrition and Dietetics Unit at Hospital Universitario San Cecilio in Granada. Her expertise in the field is complemented by her leadership role within the hospital, where she oversees the clinical nutrition and dietetics services."}{"title": "DRA. \u00c1NGELA GONZ\u00c1LEZ D\u00cdAZ-FAES:Dra. \u00c1ngela Gonz\u00e1lez D\u00edaz-Faes is a medical professional specializing in endocrinology and nutrition at Hospital Universitario Marqu\u00e9s de Valdecilla in Cantabria. She manages nutritional care for patients with diabetes and other related conditions, providing essential nutritional support specifically for diabetic patients suffering from head and neck cancer. Her expertise encompasses a comprehensive approach to nutritional management, ensuring that her patients receive tailored care to address their unique health needs."}{"title": "DR. MIGUEL LE\u00d3N SANZ:Dr. Miguel Le\u00f3n Sanz is a prominent figure in the medical field, recognized for his contributions to endocrinology and nutrition. He serves as the head of the endocrinology and nutrition service at Hospital Universitario 12 de Octubre in Madrid, where he plays a crucial role in advancing medical practices and research in these specialties. Additionally, Dr. Le\u00f3n Sanz is an author, further demonstrating his commitment to the dissemination of knowledge within the medical community."}{"title": "DR. FRANCISCO LOSFABLOS CALLAU:Dr. Francisco Losfablos Callau is a medical specialist in endocrinology and nutrition, currently practicing at Hospital Universitario Miguel Servet in Zaragoza. He is recognized for his expertise in the field and has contributed to the medical community as a co-author of articles focused on diabetes mellitus."}{"title": "DR. DANIEL A. DE LUIS ROM\u00c1N:Dr. Daniel A. de Luis Rom\u00e1n is the scientific director and head of the endocrinology and nutrition service at Hospital Cl\u00ednico Universitario de Valladolid. In this role, he oversees the department's operations and contributes to advancements in the field of endocrinology and nutrition."}{"title": "DRA. \u00c1NGELA MART\u00cdN PALMERO:Dra. \u00c1ngela Mart\u00edn Palmero is the head of the Clinical Nutrition and Dietetics Unit at Hospital San Pedro in La Rioja. In her role, she emphasizes the management of diabetes and addresses issues related to disease-related malnutrition, ensuring comprehensive care for her patients."}{"title": "DR. JUAN FRANCISCO MERINO TORRES:Dr. Juan Francisco Merino Torres is a distinguished medical doctor specializing in endocrinology and nutrition. He serves as the head of the Endocrinology and Nutrition department at Hospital Universitario y Polit\u00e9cnico La Fe in Valencia, where he also holds the position of director cient\u00edfico. Dr. Merino Torres is recognized for his expertise in the field, particularly in relation to diabetes mellitus, and has contributed to the medical community through various published articles on the subject. His leadership at the hospital underscores his commitment to advancing the understanding and treatment of endocrine and nutritional disorders."}{"title": "DRA. ROSA M\u00aa MIRETE L\u00d3PEZ:Dra. Rosa M\u00aa Mirete L\u00f3pez is a medical specialist in endocrinology and nutrition at Hospital Universitario de San Juan in Alicante. She is known for her expertise in treating patients with diabetes mellitus and inflammatory bowel disease, providing specialized care to manage these conditions effectively."}{"title": "DRA. MAR\u00cdA JOS\u00c9 MOLINA PUERTA:Dra. Mar\u00eda Jos\u00e9 Molina Puerta is a medical specialist in endocrinology and nutrition at Hospital Universitario Reina Sof\u00eda in C\u00f3rdoba. She is also an author of a clinical case that discusses the interrelated issues of morbid obesity, diabetes, and bariatric surgery, highlighting her expertise in these critical areas of health."}{"title": "DRA. JULIA OC\u00d3N BRET\u00d3N:Dra. Julia Oc\u00f3n Bret\u00f3n is a specialist in clinical nutrition and endocrinology at the Hospital Cl\u00ednico Universitario Lozano Blesa in Zaragoza. She is responsible for the Clinical Nutrition and Dietetics Unit at this hospital, where she focuses on medical nutritional therapy."}{"title": "DR. CHRISTIAN SALOM VENDRELL:Dr. Christian Salom Vendrell is a medical doctor specializing in endocrinology and nutrition at Hospital Universitario Doctor Peset in Valencia. He focuses on providing nutritional support for patients with head and neck cancer, demonstrating his expertise in managing the dietary needs of this specific patient population. Additionally, he has been involved in clinical cases, including enteral nutrition for a diabetic patient diagnosed with laryngeal squamous cell carcinoma. Through his work, Dr. Vendrell plays a crucial role in integrating nutritional care into the treatment plans for patients facing complex health challenges."}{"title": "DR. \u00c1NGEL LUIS ABAD GONZ\u00c1LEZ:Dr. \u00c1ngel Luis Abad Gonz\u00e1lez is a medical specialist in Endocrinology and Nutrition, currently practicing at the Hospital General Universitario de Alicante. He specializes in treating patients with diabetes and other related conditions. Additionally, he is involved in clinical cases, including those related to gastrostomy."}{"title": "COMPLEJO ASISTENCIAL UNIVERSITARIO DE LE\u00d3N:"}{"title": "HOSPITAL GENERAL UNIVERSITARIO SANTA LUC\u00cdA, CARTAGENA:"}{"title": "HOSPITAL CL\u00cdNICO UNIVERSITARIO LOZANO BLESAS:Hospital Cl\u00ednico Universitario Lozano Blesa is a clinical institution located in Zaragoza, Spain. It specializes in clinical nutrition and dietetics, as well as endocrinology. The hospital is directed by Dra. Julia Oc\u00f3n Bret\u00f3n, who oversees its focus on providing comprehensive care in these medical fields."}{"title": "HOSPITAL UNIVERSITARIO DOCTOR PESET:Hospital Universitario Doctor Peset is a medical institution located in Valencia, Spain, that specializes in endocrinology and nutrition."}{"title": "HOSPITAL GENERAL UNIVERSITARIO DE VALENCIA:The Hospital General Universitario de Valencia is a medical facility located in Valencia, where Dr. Carlos S\u00e1nchez Juan serves as the head of the Endocrinology and Nutrition Service. This hospital is known for providing specialized services in the fields of endocrinology and nutrition, ensuring comprehensive care for patients in these areas."}{"title": "COMPLEJO ASISTENCIAL UNIVERSITARIO DE SALAMANCA:The Complejo Asistencial Universitario de Salamanca is a healthcare facility that specializes in endocrinology and nutrition. It serves as a significant institution in the region, providing specialized medical care in these fields. Additionally, it is the workplace of Dra. Ana Isabel S\u00e1nchez Marcos, a professional associated with the facility."}{"title": "HOSPITAL UNIVERSITARIO DE BURGOS:The Hospital Universitario de Burgos is a medical institution that specializes in endocrinology and nutrition. It is also the workplace of Estefan\u00eda Santos Mazo, who practices at this hospital."}{"title": "HOSPITAL UNIVERSITARIO MIGUEL SERVET:Hospital Universitario Miguel Servet is a clinical institution located in Zaragoza, Spain, specializing in clinical nutrition and dietetics. The hospital is particularly focused on providing care for diabetic patients. Dr. Alejandro Sanz Par\u00eds serves as the head of the Clinical Nutrition and Dietetics Unit at this facility, overseeing its operations and ensuring the delivery of specialized nutritional care."}{"title": "HOSPITAL GENERAL UNIVERSITARIO JOS\u00c9 M. MORALES MESEGUER:Hospital General Universitario Jos\u00e9 M. Morales Meseguer is a hospital in Murcia specializing in endocrinology and nutrition."}{"title": "HOSPITAL UNIVERSITARIO DE ARABA:Hospital Universitario de Araba (HUA) is a hospital located in Vitoria-Gasteiz specializing in endocrinology and nutrition."}{"title": "COMPLEJO HOSPITALARIO DE TORREC\u00c1RDENAS:Complejo Hospitalario de Torrec\u00e1rdenas is a hospital in Almer\u00eda specializing in endocrinology and nutrition."}{"title": "HOSPITAL ROYO VILLANOVA:Hospital Royo Villanova is a medical facility located in Zaragoza, Spain. It specializes in various health services, with a particular focus on endocrinology and nutrition. The hospital is recognized for its expertise in these areas, providing comprehensive care to patients in need of specialized medical attention."}{"title": "HOSPITAL UNIVERSITARIO CENTRAL DE ASTURIAS:The Hospital Universitario Central de Asturias is a prominent medical facility located in Oviedo, Spain. It specializes in endocrinology and nutrition, providing comprehensive healthcare services in these fields. Among its esteemed staff is Dr. Francisco Villaz\u00f3n Gonz\u00e1lez, who serves as a specialist in endocrinology and nutrition, contributing to the hospital's reputation for excellence in patient care and medical expertise."}{"title": "DR. CARLOS S\u00c1NCHEZ JUAN:Dr. Carlos S\u00e1nchez Juan is a medical doctor who serves as the head of the Endocrinology and Nutrition department at Hospital General Universitario de Valencia. He holds the position of director cient\u00edfico and is responsible for overseeing the Endocrinology and Nutrition Service at the same hospital. His leadership role encompasses both clinical and scientific aspects of the department, highlighting his expertise and commitment to the field of endocrinology and nutrition."}{"title": "DRA. ANA ISABEL S\u00c1NCHEZ MARCOS:Dra. Ana Isabel S\u00e1nchez Marcos is a specialist in endocrinology and nutrition at Complejo Asistencial Universitario de Salamanca."}{"title": "DRA. ESTEFAN\u00cdA SANTOS MAZO:Dra. Estefan\u00eda Santos Mazo is a specialist in endocrinology and nutrition at Hospital Universitario de Burgos."}{"title": "DR. ALEJANDRO SANZ PAR\u00cdS:Dr. Alejandro Sanz Par\u00eds is the Director T\u00e9cnico and head of the Clinical Nutrition and Dietetics Unit at Hospital Universitario Miguel Servet in Zaragoza. He oversees the clinical nutrition and dietetics section, where he is responsible for managing and directing the unit's activities and ensuring the delivery of high-quality nutritional care."}{"title": "DRA. YAMINA SULEIMAN MARTOS:Dra. Yamina Suleiman Martos is a specialist in endocrinology and nutrition at Hospital General Universitario Jos\u00e9 M. Morales Meseguer in Murcia. She is also an author of a clinical case that addresses the relationship between diabetes and malabsorption, showcasing her expertise in the field of endocrinology and her contributions to medical literature."}{"title": "DRA. SARA VALLE RODR\u00cdGUEZ-NAVAS:Dra. Sara Valle Rodr\u00edguez-Navas is a medical professional specializing in endocrinology and nutrition, currently practicing at Hospital Universitario de Araba in Vitoria-Gasteiz. She focuses on nutritional management for patients with type 1 diabetes and also provides care for individuals with rumination syndrome. Her expertise lies in managing the nutritional needs of these patients, ensuring they receive appropriate dietary guidance to support their health conditions."}{"title": "DRA. MERCEDES V\u00c1ZQUEZ GUTI\u00c9RREZ:Dra. Mercedes V\u00e1zquez Guti\u00e9rrez is a specialist in endocrinology and nutrition at Complejo Hospitalario de Torrec\u00e1rdenas in Almer\u00eda. She is also an author of a clinical case that examines a patient with pancreatic intraductal papillary mucinous neoplasm, with a particular focus on issues of malnutrition and secondary diabetes."}{"title": "DRA. CONCEPCI\u00d3N VIDAL PERACHO:Dra. Concepci\u00f3n Vidal Peracho is a medical professional specializing in endocrinology and nutrition, currently practicing at Hospital Royo Villanova in Zaragoza. She focuses on the treatment of patients with diabetes, particularly type 1 diabetes, and emphasizes the importance of nutrition in managing cancer treatment for these patients. Dra. Vidal Peracho utilizes a continuous subcutaneous insulin infusion device as part of her approach to care, integrating her expertise in both nutrition and endocrinology to provide comprehensive support for her patients."}{"title": "DR. FRANCISCO VILLAZ\u00d3N GONZ\u00c1LEZ:Dr. Francisco Villaz\u00f3n Gonz\u00e1lez is a specialist in endocrinology and nutrition at Hospital Universitario Central de Asturias in Oviedo."}{"title": "DR. JUAN BAUTISTA MOLINA SORIA:Dr. Juan Bautista Molina Soria is the technical director and head of the Clinical Nutrition and Dietetics Unit at Hospital Universitario San Agust\u00edn, located in Linares, Ja\u00e9n."}{"title": "DRA. MERCEDES V\u00c1ZQUEZ(\"ENTITY\":"}{"title": "HOSPITAL UNIVERSITARIO SAN CECILIO:HOSPITAL UNIVERSITARIO SAN CECILIO is a university hospital situated in Granada, Spain. It specializes in a range of medical fields, with a particular focus on endocrinology and nutrition."}{"title": "HOSPITAL UNIVERSITARIO SAN AGUST\u00cdN:Hospital Universitario San Agust\u00edn is a university hospital situated in Linares, Ja\u00e9n, Spain. It specializes in clinical nutrition and dietetics, with Dr. Juan Bautista Molina Soria serving as the head of the Clinical Nutrition and Dietetics Unit. The hospital is dedicated to providing comprehensive healthcare services, emphasizing the importance of nutrition in patient care."}{"title": "HOSPITAL UNIVERSITARIO Y POLIT\u00c9CNICO LA FE:HOSPITAL UNIVERSITARIO Y POLIT\u00c9CNICO LA FE is a hospital located in Valencia, Spain. Dr. Juan Francisco Merino Torres serves as the head of the Endocrinology and Nutrition Service at this institution. He is responsible for overseeing the department, which focuses on the diagnosis and treatment of endocrine disorders and nutritional issues."}{"title": "HOSPITAL SAN PEDRO:Hospital San Pedro is a healthcare facility located in La Rioja, where Dr. \u00c1ngela Mart\u00edn Palmero serves as the head of the Clinical Nutrition and Dietetics Unit. This clinical institution is dedicated to providing specialized care in the fields of clinical nutrition and dietetics, under the expert direction of Dr. Mart\u00edn Palmero."}{"title": "HOSPITAL CL\u00cdNICO UNIVERSITARIO LOZANO BLES:A hospital in Zaragoza where Dr. Julia Oc\u00f3n Bret\u00f3n is the head of the Clinical Nutrition and Dietetics Unit."}{"title": "DR. \u00c1NGELA MART\u00cdN PALMERO:Director cient\u00edfica and head of the Clinical Nutrition and Dietetics Unit at Hospital San Pedro."}{"title": "DR. JULIA OC\u00d3N BRET\u00d3N:Director cient\u00edfica and head of the Clinical Nutrition and Dietetics Unit at Hospital Cl\u00ednico Universitario Lozano Blesa."}{"title": "MESA REDONDA DE CASOS CL\u00cdNICOS. NORTE:A round table event discussing clinical cases related to nutrition and diabetes management."}{"title": "FIBROSIS QU\u00cdSTICA:Fibrosis qu\u00edstica, also known as cystic fibrosis, is a genetic disorder that primarily affects the lungs and digestive system. It is caused by a mutation in the CFTR gene and is inherited in an autosomal recessive manner. The condition was diagnosed in the patient at the age of 2 and is characterized by a range of complications, including malnutrition and diabetes, which can significantly worsen the patient's prognosis. Due to the complexity of the disease, it necessitates multidisciplinary management and specialized nutritional care to address the various health challenges faced by affected individuals."}{"title": "ENFERMEDAD INFLAMATORIA INTESTINAL:Enfermedad Inflamatoria Intestinal refers to a group of inflammatory conditions affecting the gastrointestinal tract. These conditions may necessitate specific dietary interventions to manage symptoms and improve patient outcomes. Additionally, Enfermedad Inflamatoria Intestinal should be considered in the differential diagnosis of mitochondrial diseases, highlighting its relevance in a broader medical context."}{"title": "C\u00c1NCER DE CABEZA Y CUELLO:C\u00c1NCER DE CABEZA Y CUELLO refers to a type of cancer that affects the head and neck region. This form of cancer often necessitates nutritional support during treatment due to the challenges it poses in these areas. Specifically, it includes conditions such as carcinoma epidermoide of the hemilangue, which is a type of squamous cell carcinoma that can occur in the oral cavity. Overall, C\u00c1NCER DE CABEZA Y CUELLO encompasses various malignancies within the head and neck, highlighting the importance of comprehensive care and support for affected patients."}{"title": "C\u00c1NCER DE P\u00c1NCREAS:C\u00c1NCER DE P\u00c1NCREAS is a serious and aggressive form of cancer that affects the pancreas. It is characterized by a low survival rate and is often diagnosed at a late stage due to the absence of early symptoms. Patients diagnosed with this type of cancer require careful nutritional management to support their health and treatment."}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N ENTERAL:NUTRICI\u00d3N ENTERAL, or enteral nutrition (NE), is a medical method of feeding that delivers nutrients directly into the gastrointestinal tract, bypassing the usual process of eating and digestion. This approach is particularly beneficial for patients who are unable to eat by mouth due to various medical conditions, including swallowing difficulties, severe caloric malnutrition, diabetes, rumination syndrome, and complications following surgery. \n\nEnteral nutrition is often administered through a nasogastric tube or via a gastrostomy, such as a percutaneous endoscopic gastrostomy (PEG), to ensure that patients receive the necessary nutrients when oral intake is insufficient. It is commonly used in the management of conditions like cystic fibrosis and severe acute pancreatitis, where it can improve clinical outcomes and reduce mortality rates. \n\nThe method is preferred over parenteral nutrition in many cases, especially for patients undergoing digestive surgery, as it utilizes the gastrointestinal tract effectively. Overall, enteral nutrition serves as a crucial nutritional support system tailored to meet the specific dietary needs of patients who cannot consume food orally, thereby enhancing their nutritional status and overall health."}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N CL\u00cdNICA:NUTRICI\u00d3N CL\u00cdNICA refers to the field of clinical nutrition, which encompasses the assessment and management of dietary needs and nutritional therapy for patients with a variety of health conditions. This discipline applies nutritional knowledge to effectively manage patients' dietary requirements within clinical settings, ensuring that individuals receive appropriate nutritional support tailored to their specific health issues."}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N ARTIFICIAL:NUTRICI\u00d3N ARTIFICIAL refers to a medical treatment that delivers nutrition through methods other than traditional eating, making it particularly beneficial for patients who have severe dietary restrictions. This approach is essential for individuals who cannot consume food orally due to various medical conditions. However, it is important to note that artificial nutrition can lead to complications, such as diabetes, especially in patients with specific conditions like MELAS syndrome. Thus, while NUTRICI\u00d3N ARTIFICIAL serves a critical role in patient care, it also necessitates careful management to mitigate potential health risks."}{"title": "DIETA TERAP\u00c9UTICA:A specialized diet designed to manage specific health conditions, such as diabetes or cancer.)<|COMPLETE|>"}{"title": "MIGUEL LE\u00d3N SANZ:Miguel Le\u00f3n Sanz is the President of the Sociedad Espa\u00f1ola de Nutrici\u00f3n Cl\u00ednica y Metabolismo (SENPE) and is involved in the field of clinical nutrition and metabolism."}{"title": "SOCIEDAD ESPA\u00d1OLA DE NUTRICI\u00d3N CL\u00cdNICA Y METABOLISMO:The Sociedad Espa\u00f1ola de Nutrici\u00f3n Cl\u00ednica y Metabolismo (SENPE) is an organization focused on improving clinical nutrition and metabolism practices in Spain."}{"title": "DIABETES MELLITUS:Diabetes Mellitus is a chronic health condition that significantly impacts the body's ability to regulate and process blood sugar (glucose). It is characterized by high blood sugar levels, which can arise from insulin resistance or insufficient insulin production. This condition is prevalent in various populations and is often associated with other clinical conditions, including acute pancreatitis and neoplasias. \n\nDiabetes Mellitus is particularly notable for its complications, which can include malnutrition, pressure ulcers in elderly patients, and other serious health issues if not managed properly. It is a significant public health concern in the 21st century, with increasing prevalence and a growing burden on healthcare systems. The condition often requires specialized dietary management and insulin therapy to control blood sugar levels effectively.\n\nIn specific cases, such as in patients with MELAS (Mitochondrial Encephalomyopathy, Lactic Acidosis, and Stroke-like episodes), Diabetes Mellitus can manifest as an endocrine complication, affecting metabolic health and often diagnosed in early adulthood. The condition can also complicate the management of other health issues, highlighting the need for coordinated efforts in prevention and control.\n\nDiagnosis of Diabetes Mellitus typically involves identifying elevated glucose levels and insulin resistance, and it may require treatment with oral antidiabetic medications. The condition is recognized as a risk factor for malnutrition, particularly in patients with cancer, and underscores the importance of regular treatment adherence to prevent complications."}{"title": "ENFERMEDADES:Diseases refer to various health conditions that may coexist with diabetes, affecting the patient's nutritional needs and treatment."}{"title": "TRATAMIENTO NUTRICIONAL:Nutritional treatment involves dietary management tailored to the specific needs of patients, especially those with diabetes and other diseases."}{"title": "HEMOGLOBINA GLICOSILADA:Glycated hemoglobin is a blood test that reflects average blood sugar levels over the past three months, important for managing diabetes."}{"title": "GRADUADOS EN NUTRICI\u00d3N HUMANA Y DIET\u00c9TICA:Graduates in Human Nutrition and Dietetics are professionals trained to provide dietary advice and nutritional therapy."}{"title": "ESPECIALISTAS EN ENDOCRINOLOG\u00cdA Y NUTRICI\u00d3N:Specialists in Endocrinology and Nutrition are healthcare professionals with expertise in hormonal and nutritional management of patients."}{"title": "OBJETIVOS NUTRICIONALES:Nutritional objectives are specific dietary goals set for patients to improve their health outcomes, particularly in managing diabetes."}{"title": "FORMACI\u00d3N EN NUTRICI\u00d3N CL\u00cdNICA:Training in clinical nutrition is essential for healthcare professionals to effectively manage patients' dietary needs."}{"title": "PACIENTE:The patient is an individual diagnosed with multiple health conditions, including adenocarcinoma of the pancreas, moderate to severe acute pancreatitis, obesity (grade 1), and type 2 diabetes that was previously controlled. Throughout their medical journey, the patient has experienced a range of symptoms and treatments, including fluctuations in glucose levels and varying insulin requirements. They have also received nutritional support due to complications such as a pancreatic fistula and severe malnutrition.\n\nIn addition to these conditions, the patient has been diagnosed with dysphagia secondary to a chronic swallowing disorder post-radiotherapy, leading to moderate caloric-protein malnutrition. They have shown symptoms of rumination syndrome and have undergone multiple treatments to manage this condition. The patient has a history of chronic health issues, including diabetes and liver complications, resulting in significant weight loss over the years.\n\nThe patient is a 48-year-old individual with insulin-dependent type 2 diabetes and morbid obesity who underwent gastric bypass surgery. They have also received enteral and parenteral nutrition due to short bowel syndrome and previously undiagnosed diabetes. Post-surgery, the patient faced complications but has shown health improvements with nutritional support through a PEG (percutaneous endoscopic gastrostomy).\n\nAdditionally, the patient has a history of eating disorders and is currently undergoing evaluation and treatment for both diabetes and these disorders. They are also diagnosed with severe caloric malnutrition, experiencing significant weight loss and gastrointestinal issues, necessitating nutritional intervention via a nasogastric tube. \n\nThe patient is a young woman with Type 1 Diabetes (DM1) and an eating disorder, receiving treatment and monitoring for both conditions. They are also undergoing treatment for a head and neck neoplasm, ischemic stroke, and severe complications related to Crohn's disease, which have involved multiple surgeries and nutritional challenges. Furthermore, the patient has cystic fibrosis and has undergone various nutritional interventions and health monitoring.\n\nOverall, the patient is receiving comprehensive medical care for their complex health issues, including diabetes management, nutritional support, and treatment for various chronic conditions. They are currently being evaluated for metabolic surgery and are experiencing partial remission of diabetes, while also undergoing various nutritional therapies and surgical procedures to address swallowing difficulties and nutritional needs."}{"title": "HOSPITAL CL\u00cdNICO UNIVERSITARIO LOZANO BLESA:The University Clinical Hospital Lozano Blesa in Zaragoza provides healthcare services and is involved in clinical nutrition and dietetics."}{"title": "ZARAGOZA:Zaragoza is a city in Spain where the University Clinical Hospital Lozano Blesa is located."}{"title": "PREDYCES:PREDYCES is a comprehensive study conducted in hospitals across Spain, focusing on the nutritional status of oncology patients and assessing the prevalence of disease-related malnutrition among this demographic. The research revealed significant rates of malnutrition both upon admission and discharge of patients. Additionally, the PREDYCES study involved the nutritional assessment of diabetic patients in 50 hospitals, further highlighting the critical issue of malnutrition in hospitalized individuals. Overall, PREDYCES underscores the urgent need to address malnutrition in oncology and diabetic patients within the hospital setting."}{"title": "EUROPE:Europe is a continent facing several significant health concerns, including a high prevalence of diabetes, which affects millions of individuals. Additionally, disease-related malnutrition is a major public health issue within the region. Furthermore, Europe has been the focus of various studies and surveys related to cystic fibrosis, highlighting the continent's ongoing efforts to address and understand these health challenges."}{"title": "SPAIN:Spain is a country located in Southern Europe, recognized for its significant public health challenges, particularly concerning the increasing prevalence of diabetes mellitus. It ranks fourth in Europe for the number of individuals affected by diabetes, highlighting the urgency of addressing this health issue. Various studies have been conducted in Spain to explore diabetes prevalence and management, including a notable study by Olveira et al. that focused on enteral nutrition and diabetes in hospitalized patients. Additionally, Spain is the site of the PREDYCES study, which estimates the costs associated with disease-related malnutrition. Overall, Spain's health landscape is marked by a critical need for effective diabetes management and nutritional interventions."}{"title": "SOPORTE NUTRICIONAL ESPECIALIZADO:Specialized nutritional support refers to medical nutritional therapy that includes oral nutritional supplements, enteral nutrition, and parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "SNO:SNO refers to oral nutritional supplements designed to support the dietary needs of patients, particularly those at risk of malnutrition. These specialized nutritional supplements are administered orally and are particularly beneficial for patients with malnutrition, those preparing for surgery, and individuals managing diabetes. SNO encompasses a range of nutritional formulas tailored to enhance dietary intake, providing essential calories and nutrients necessary for recovery and overall health. Additionally, SNO includes specific nutritional support for patients undergoing cancer treatment, ensuring that their unique dietary requirements are met. Overall, SNO plays a crucial role in improving the nutritional status of patients in various medical contexts."}{"title": "MALNUTRICI\u00d3N RELACIONADA CON LA ENFERMEDAD:MALNUTRICI\u00d3N RELACIONADA CON LA ENFERMEDAD, also known as disease-related malnutrition (DRE), is a condition characterized by a compromised nutritional status in patients due to illness. This condition significantly impacts clinical outcomes and contributes to increased healthcare costs. DRE is recognized as a major public health issue, particularly in developed countries, where it is associated with heightened risks of morbidity and mortality."}{"title": "PACIENTES GERI\u00c1TRICOS:Geriatric patients are a specific group particularly affected by disease-related malnutrition, as highlighted in the PREDYCES study."}{"title": "PACIENTES ONCOL\u00d3GICOS:Oncological patients are another group at high risk for disease-related malnutrition, as indicated by the findings of the PREDYCES study."}{"title": "ENFERMOS MAYORES DE 70 A\u00d1OS:Patients over 70 years old are significantly affected by disease-related malnutrition, with a prevalence of 37% according to the PREDYCES study."}{"title": "DISFAGIA:Disfagia, also known as dysphagia, is a medical condition characterized by difficulty swallowing. This condition can lead to various complications, including an increased risk of disease-related malnutrition, which affects a significant portion of hospitalized patients. In one particular case, a patient experienced disfagia, prompting a referral to the ORL (Otorhinolaryngology) department for further evaluation and management."}{"title": "POLIMEDICACI\u00d3N:Polypharmacy is a risk factor for disease-related malnutrition, particularly in elderly and complex chronic patients."}{"title": "NOURISH:The NOURISH study is a recent multicenter clinical trial examining the effects of a hyperproteic nutritional supplement enriched with beta-hydroxy-beta-methylbutyrate on malnourished elderly patients in hospitals."}{"title": "ESPEN:ESPEN, or the European Society for Clinical Nutrition and Metabolism, is a professional organization dedicated to providing comprehensive guidelines and recommendations for nutritional support across various patient populations. It focuses on patients with specific health conditions, including those with dementia, oncology patients, elderly individuals, and those with polymorbid conditions. ESPEN emphasizes the importance of nutritional screening, assessment, and treatment, advocating for the use of oral nutritional supplements (ONS) to enhance dietary intake and mitigate complications. Additionally, the organization addresses the nutritional needs of patients with intestinal issues and provides guidance on clinical nutrition and hydration, which is particularly relevant for diabetes management. Through its efforts, ESPEN aims to improve the overall nutritional care and outcomes for patients facing diverse health challenges."}{"title": "PHILIPSON ET AL.:Philipson et al. conducted an analysis of hospital admission records of 44 million hospitalized patients in the U.S. over 11 years, focusing on the impact of oral nutritional supplements on hospital stays and readmission rates."}{"title": "ELIA ET AL.:Elia et al. published systematic reviews and meta-analyses regarding the use of oral nutritional supplements in hospitalized and community patients with various pathologies."}{"title": "BALLY ET AL.:Bally et al. conducted a systematic review and meta-analysis on nutritional support and outcomes in malnourished medical inpatients."}{"title": "HOSPITALIZATION:Hospitalization refers to the process of admitting a patient to a hospital for medical care and treatment. It encompasses the admission of patients for various types of medical interventions, and is a key context in which the benefits of oral nutritional supplements are evaluated."}{"title": "MALNOURISHED PATIENTS:Malnourished patients are individuals who are hospitalized and at risk of complications due to inadequate nutritional intake."}{"title": "HOSPITAL READMISSIONS:Hospital readmissions refer to the instances when patients return to the hospital after discharge, which is a key metric evaluated in studies regarding the effectiveness of nutritional supplements."}{"title": "NUTRITIONAL SUPPORT:Nutritional support encompasses a range of interventions designed to enhance dietary intake and improve health outcomes for patients. This practice includes the use of oral nutritional supplements and other dietary interventions aimed at managing health conditions and improving nutritional status. It is particularly important for patients who are unable to meet their nutritional needs through regular eating, such as those with complications from conditions like obesity or diabetes. Overall, nutritional support plays a crucial role in providing dietary assistance to individuals in need, ensuring they receive the necessary nutrients to support their health and recovery."}{"title": "HYPERPROTEIC NUTRITIONAL SUPPLEMENT:"}{"title": "MAR\u00cdA D. BALLESTEROS POMAR:Mar\u00eda D. Ballesteros Pomar is a medical specialist in Endocrinology and Nutrition, and the coordinator of the Nutrition Area of the SEEN at the Complejo Asistencial Universitario de Le\u00f3n."}{"title": "SEEN:The SEEN is the Spanish Society of Endocrinology and Nutrition, focusing on diabetes and nutrition-related health issues."}{"title": "CASTILLA Y LE\u00d3N:Castilla y Le\u00f3n is an autonomous community in Spain that is experiencing a notable increase in the prevalence of diabetes and related mortality rates. This region is characterized by an aging population, which contributes to the growing health concern surrounding diabetes. In response to this public health issue, clinical case conferences have been held in Castilla y Le\u00f3n to address and discuss the challenges posed by diabetes in the community. Overall, diabetes remains a significant health concern in Castilla y Le\u00f3n, highlighting the need for ongoing attention and intervention."}{"title": "IDF:The International Diabetes Federation (IDF) is an organization dedicated to providing data and advocacy related to diabetes on a global scale. It plays a crucial role in raising awareness and promoting education about diabetes through its various initiatives. One of its key contributions is the publication of the Atlas of Diabetes, which offers comprehensive global epidemiological data on the prevalence and impact of diabetes worldwide. Through these efforts, the IDF aims to improve the understanding of diabetes and support efforts to combat this growing health issue."}{"title": "XXIX CONGRESO NACIONAL DE LA SOCIEDAD ESPA\u00d1OLA DE DIABETES:The XXIX National Congress of the Spanish Diabetes Society is a significant event focused on diabetes research and awareness. During this congress, the results of the di@bet.es study were presented, highlighting important findings related to diabetes management and care. Additionally, the congress served as a platform for presenting new data on the prevalence of diabetes in Spain, contributing to the understanding of the disease's impact within the country. This event underscores the ongoing efforts of the Spanish Diabetes Society to advance knowledge and improve outcomes for individuals affected by diabetes."}{"title": "DIABETES ATLAS:The Diabetes Atlas is a publication by the IDF that provides comprehensive data on the global prevalence of diabetes."}{"title": "SOCIEDAD ESPA\u00d1OLA DE DIABETES:The Spanish Diabetes Society is an organization that focuses on diabetes research and education, hosting the XXIX National Congress to discuss diabetes prevalence and management."}{"title": "ASTURIAS:Asturias is an autonomous community in Spain, recognized as the most aged community, influencing diabetes statistics in neighboring regions."}{"title": "EMERGING RISK FACTORS COLLABORATION:The Emerging Risk Factors Collaboration is a research group that studies the impact of various health factors, including diabetes, on mortality rates."}{"title": "COHORT DE DIABETES MELLITUS DE CASTILLA Y LE\u00d3N:The Diabetes Mellitus Cohort of Castilla y Le\u00f3n is a study initiated in 2000 to track new diabetes diagnoses and their long-term health impacts."}{"title": "DIABETES:Diabetes is a chronic medical condition that significantly affects how the body processes blood sugar (glucose). It requires careful management, including specific nutritional strategies and often the use of insulin. The condition is characterized by high blood sugar levels and can lead to various complications, including an increased risk of developing pancreatic cancer and complicating the management of conditions such as pancreatitis. \n\nDiabetes has substantial implications for public health, healthcare costs, and patient resources, particularly in regions like Spain. It is also associated with other health issues, such as MELAS syndrome, which can arise from insulin resistance and deficiency. Furthermore, diabetes can contribute to serious health problems, including obesity, if not well controlled. Lifestyle changes and medical interventions are crucial for prevention and management, highlighting the importance of ongoing attention to this chronic disease."}{"title": "RIESGO DE ENFERMEDAD CARDIOVASCULAR EN CASTILLA Y LE\u00d3N:The Risk of Cardiovascular Disease in Castilla y Le\u00f3n study examines the relationship between diabetes and cardiovascular health over a decade."}{"title": "MORTALIDAD:MORTALIDAD refers to the rate of deaths in patients with acute pancreatitis, which can be influenced by the type of nutritional support provided. Additionally, mortality related to diabetes is a significant public health concern, as diabetes is one of the leading causes of death in Western countries. The increased risk of death associated with diabetes has been emphasized by various studies and statistics, highlighting the serious implications of this condition on overall mortality rates."}{"title": "POBLACI\u00d3N:The population refers to the general public in Castilla y Le\u00f3n, particularly those affected by diabetes and its related health issues."}{"title": "DIABETES MELLITUS TIPO 2:Diabetes Mellitus Tipo 2 is a prevalent form of diabetes characterized by insulin resistance, significantly impacting health interventions. It is a major health concern in Spain, with a prevalence rate of 13.8% in the general population and an incidence of 11.58 cases per 1000 people per year. This chronic condition affects how the body metabolizes glucose, leading to increased mortality risk, particularly in regions such as Castilla y Le\u00f3n.\n\nPatients with Diabetes Mellitus Tipo 2 often manage the condition over many years; for instance, one patient has been managing it for 15 years, while another has been managing it for 10 years. In some cases, the condition is insulin-dependent and poorly controlled. Despite these challenges, there are instances where the diabetes was well-controlled prior to hospitalization, and some patients have undergone surgical interventions related to their diabetes management.\n\nAdditionally, there is a familial aspect to Diabetes Mellitus Tipo 2, as indicated by a family history of the disease, such as a diagnosis in the patient's grandmother. Overall, Diabetes Mellitus Tipo 2 is a chronic metabolic disease that requires ongoing management and can lead to serious health complications if not properly controlled."}{"title": "DR. SHAUKAT SADIKOT:Dr. Shaukat Sadikot was the president of the IDF during 2016-2017 and emphasized the global crisis of diabetes."}{"title": "ESPANA:Spain, known as \"ESPANA,\" is a country that has been experiencing a general decrease in diabetes mortality rates, although this trend contrasts with the situation in the region of Castilla y Le\u00f3n, where the rates may not reflect the same improvement. Additionally, Spain is actively engaged in studies focused on diabetes prevalence and healthcare costs, which underscore the socio-economic impact of diabetes on its population. These efforts indicate a commitment to understanding and addressing the challenges posed by diabetes within the country."}{"title": "SISTEMA NACIONAL DE SALUD:The National Health System in Spain is responsible for healthcare delivery, including diabetes treatment and management."}{"title": "GASTO SANITARIO:Healthcare spending related to diabetes in Spain, which includes both direct and indirect costs associated with the disease."}{"title": "EUROPA:EUROPA, the continent of Europe, has a notable incidence of cystic fibrosis, occurring in one in every 3,500 births, which translates to a mean prevalence of 0.8 cases per 10,000 inhabitants. Additionally, Europe faces significant healthcare challenges related to diabetes, with a considerable portion of health budgets dedicated to addressing this condition."}{"title": "COSTES INDIRECTOS:Indirect costs associated with diabetes, including absenteeism and early retirements, which impact the economy."}{"title": "COSTES DIRECTOS:Direct costs related to diabetes treatments and hospitalizations, which are a significant part of healthcare expenditure."}{"title": "PRESIDENTE DE LA IDF:The title refers to the leader of the International Diabetes Federation, who plays a crucial role in advocating for diabetes awareness and management."}{"title": "COHORTE DE DIABETES MELLITUS DE CASTILLA Y LE\u00d3N:CODICYL is a diabetes cohort study in the region of Castilla y Le\u00f3n, Spain, focusing on diabetes-related health issues and outcomes."}{"title": "FEDERACI\u00d3N ESPA\u00d1OLA DE DIABETES:FEDE is a Spanish federation that provides resources and information about diabetes, aiming to improve the quality of life for people with diabetes in Spain."}{"title": "ALEJANDRO SANZ PAR\u00cdS:Dr. Alejandro Sanz Par\u00eds is a medical professional specializing in nutrition and dietetics, with a focus on diabetes care at Hospital Universitario Miguel Servet in Zaragoza. He serves as the technical director and head of the Clinical Nutrition and Dietetics Unit at the hospital, where he plays a crucial role in managing and overseeing nutritional care for patients."}{"title": "FRANCISCO LOSFABLOS CALLAU:Dr. Francisco Losfablos Callau is a medical professional specializing in nutrition and dietetics, working alongside Dr. Alejandro Sanz Par\u00eds at Hospital Universitario Miguel Servet."}{"title": "OMS:The OMS, or World Health Organization (WHO), is a specialized agency of the United Nations dedicated to international public health. It plays a crucial role in providing data on various health issues, including the prevalence of diabetes worldwide. Additionally, the WHO is responsible for establishing guidelines for the classification of diseases, thereby contributing to global health standards and practices."}{"title": "OLVEIRA ET AL.:Olveira et al. conducted a study in Spain that focused on two main aspects related to hospitalized patients, particularly those with diabetes. The first aspect of their research observed the prevalence of enteral nutrition among these patients, highlighting its significance in their care. Additionally, the study examined the costs associated with diabetes care in hospitalized patients, providing insights into the financial implications of managing diabetes in a hospital setting. Through their comprehensive analysis, Olveira et al. contributed valuable information to the understanding of nutritional and economic factors affecting diabetes care in Spain."}{"title": "DIABETES TIPO 1:Type 1 diabetes is a form of diabetes characterized by the body's inability to produce insulin. This condition necessitates lifelong management and treatment to maintain blood glucose levels within a healthy range."}{"title": "DIABETES TIPO 2:Diabetes tipo 2 is a chronic medical condition that has affected the patient for 12 years, primarily linked to obesity and challenges in glucose control. This form of diabetes is characterized by insulin resistance and is often associated with lifestyle factors, making it a significant health concern. It is prevalent in Spain and has implications for healthcare resources and costs. The increasing prevalence of diabetes tipo 2, particularly among older populations, highlights the need for effective management strategies, including the recommendation of metabolic surgery for obese patients. Overall, diabetes tipo 2 represents a major public health issue that requires ongoing attention and intervention."}{"title": "SANZ PARIS ET AL.:Sanz Par\u00eds et al. conducted a significant study in 2013 on malnutrition prevalence among hospitalized diabetic patients in Spain."}{"title": "NRS-2002:NRS-2002 is a nutritional risk screening tool used in the Predyces study to assess malnutrition among diabetic patients."}{"title": "MNA:The MNA, or Mini Nutritional Assessment, is a validated method designed for nutritional screening in individuals over the age of 65. It serves as a crucial tool for evaluating the risk of malnutrition among various patient populations, including those with diabetes. This comprehensive assessment helps identify nutritional deficiencies and supports the development of appropriate interventions to improve the health and well-being of older adults."}{"title": "COSTES DE ATENCI\u00d3N DE LA SALUD:Healthcare costs associated with diabetes in Spain, which were studied to understand the economic impact of the disease."}{"title": "HOSPITALES:Hospitals in Spain where studies on diabetes and malnutrition among patients are conducted."}{"title": "GASTO TOTAL DEL SISTEMA NACIONAL DE SALUD:Total expenditure of the National Health System in Spain, which includes costs related to diabetes management."}{"title": "\u00daLCERAS DE DEC\u00daBITO:Pressure ulcers that are a significant concern for diabetic patients, as highlighted in various studies."}{"title": "RIESGO DE AMPUTACI\u00d3N:Risk of amputation associated with diabetes, particularly in patients with diabetic foot complications."}{"title": "MEDICARE:Medicare is a U.S. federal health insurance program that provides coverage primarily for individuals aged 65 and older, as well as some younger individuals with disabilities. The program is designed to assist with healthcare costs and has been involved in studies related to various health conditions, including diabetes and malnutrition. Medicare offers essential support for individuals with diabetes and other medical conditions, ensuring access to necessary healthcare services."}{"title": "HOSPITAL:The hospital is a comprehensive healthcare institution that provides a wide range of medical services and treatments to patients. It is where individuals receive medical attention for various conditions, including consultations in endocrinology and nutrition, as well as surgical and medical treatments. The hospital plays a crucial role in the management of serious illnesses, such as adenocarcinoma of the pancreas, where it facilitates patient admissions and palliative care. Additionally, it offers specialized care for patients with neurodegenerative diseases, including Alzheimer's, and supports those with metabolic disorders like diabetes and malnutrition. The hospital is also equipped to provide multidisciplinary care for patients with Mitochondrial Neurogastrointestinal Encephalomyopathy (MNGIE), which includes nutritional support and evaluations for potential transplants. Furthermore, it serves as a critical facility for urgent medical situations, such as the evaluation and treatment of strokes, ensuring that patients receive timely and appropriate care for their conditions. Overall, the hospital is a vital institution dedicated to the health and well-being of its patients through a variety of medical services and treatments."}{"title": "GERIATRIC RESIDENCE:Geriatric residences are facilities that provide care for elderly individuals, often focusing on their specific health needs, including diabetes management and nutritional support."}{"title": "MALNUTRICI\u00d3N:Malnutrici\u00f3n is a condition that affects individuals, characterized by an inadequate intake of nutrients. It occurs when a person's diet fails to provide sufficient nutrients, which is particularly concerning for diabetic patients, especially in geriatric care. Malnutrici\u00f3n related to disease is a significant issue in hospitalized patients with diabetes, as it can adversely impact morbidity and mortality rates."}{"title": "ALHAMBRA PRISON:Alhambra Prison is a facility where patients with diabetes may be treated for related health issues, although it is not explicitly mentioned in the text, it represents a type of institution relevant to the context."}{"title": "EUROPEAN COUNTRIES:European countries are referenced in the context of a study involving elderly patients and diabetes, highlighting the geographical scope of the research."}{"title": "HOSPITAL UNIVERSITARIO PUERTA DEL MAR:Hospital Universitario Puerta del Mar is a hospital located in C\u00e1diz, Spain, involved in diabetes research and treatment."}{"title": "JUAN OLIVA:Juan Oliva is a researcher who has contributed to studies on the direct health care costs of diabetic patients in Spain."}{"title": "F\u00c9LIX LOBO:F\u00e9lix Lobo is a researcher involved in diabetes care studies in Spain."}{"title": "BEGO\u00d1A MOLINA:Bego\u00f1a Molina is a researcher who has worked on diabetes-related health care costs in Spain."}{"title": "SUSANA MONEREO:Susana Monereo is a researcher contributing to studies on diabetes in Spain."}{"title": "MIGUEL RUIZ-RAMOS:Miguel Ruiz-Ramos is a researcher focused on diabetes mortality, prevalence, and economic costs in Spain."}{"title": "ANTONIO ESCOLAR-PUJOLAR:Antonio Escolar-Pujolar is a researcher involved in diabetes studies in Spain."}{"title": "EDUARDO MAYORAL-SANCH\u00c9Z:Eduardo Mayoral-Sanch\u00e9z is a researcher studying diabetes in Spain."}{"title": "FLORENTINO CORRAL LAUREANO:Florentino Corral Laureano is a researcher who has contributed to diabetes studies in Spain."}{"title": "ISABEL FERN\u00c1NDEZ-FERN\u00c1NDEZ:Isabel Fern\u00e1ndez-Fern\u00e1ndez is a researcher involved in diabetes research in Spain."}{"title": "SANZ PAR\u00cdS A:Sanz Par\u00eds A is a researcher studying malnutrition prevalence in hospitalized elderly diabetic patients."}{"title": "GARC\u00cdA JM:Garc\u00eda JM is a researcher involved in studies on malnutrition in diabetic patients."}{"title": "GOMEZ-CANDELA C:Gomez-Candela C is a researcher studying malnutrition in hospitalized diabetic patients."}{"title": "BURGOS R:Burgos R is a researcher contributing to studies on malnutrition in diabetic patients."}{"title": "MART\u00cdN A:Mart\u00edn A is a researcher involved in studies on malnutrition in elderly diabetic patients."}{"title": "MAT\u00cdA P:Mat\u00eda P is a researcher studying malnutrition in hospitalized diabetic patients."}{"title": "GLUCOSE REGULATION:Impaired glucose regulation is a condition related to diabetes that affects how the body manages blood sugar levels, as discussed in the studies."}{"title": "HOSPITAL DISCHARGE RECORDS:Hospital discharge records are documents that summarize a patient's hospital stay and are mentioned in the context of under-reporting diabetes prevalence."}{"title": "INPATIENT GLYCEMIC CONTROL:Inpatient glycemic control refers to the management of blood sugar levels in hospitalized patients, a topic covered in the studies."}{"title": "MALNUTRITION:Malnutrition is a condition that arises from an unbalanced diet and can significantly impact various patient populations. It is particularly concerning for individuals with MELAS syndrome, as their specific nutritional needs must be carefully managed to prevent complications. Additionally, malnutrition is a critical issue for diabetic patients, especially among the elderly, who may face unique dietary challenges. This condition has been the subject of numerous studies aimed at understanding its effects and finding effective interventions for those at risk."}{"title": "AMERICAN ASSOCIATION OF CLINICAL ENDOCRINOLOGISTS:The American Association of Clinical Endocrinologists is a professional organization that provides guidelines and consensus statements on diabetes management."}{"title": "AMERICAN DIABETES ASSOCIATION:The American Diabetes Association is a prominent organization dedicated to diabetes care and research. It plays a crucial role in providing guidelines and recommendations for effective diabetes management. Additionally, the association is involved in diabetes research and education, offering valuable resources to support individuals and healthcare professionals in managing diabetes effectively."}{"title": "DIABETES RESEARCH AND CLINICAL PRACTICE:Diabetes Research and Clinical Practice is a journal that publishes studies related to diabetes management and research."}{"title": "ARCHIVES OF INTERNAL MEDICINE:Archives of Internal Medicine is a journal that publishes research articles, including those related to diabetes and its complications."}{"title": "NUTRITION HOSPITAL:Nutrition Hospital refers to the context of studies focusing on the nutritional aspects of diabetes management in hospitalized patients.)<|COMPLETE|>"}{"title": "STUDY VIDA:Study VIDA group focuses on the application of the new ESPEN definition of malnutrition in geriatric diabetic patients during hospitalization."}{"title": "PREDYCES STUDY:The PREDyCES Study analyzes the prevalence of hospital malnutrition in patients with diabetes mellitus."}{"title": "PAN-EUROPEAN PRESSURE ULCER STUDY:A study that investigates intrinsic and extrinsic risk factors for hip fractures and pressure ulcers across Europe."}{"title": "BMC GERIATRICS:A journal that publishes research on co-morbidities and the development of pressure ulcers among older adults."}{"title": "NATIONAL MEDICARE PATIENT SAFETY MONITORING SYSTEM:A system that monitors hospital-acquired pressure ulcers in Medicare patients."}{"title": "SHELTER STUDY:The SHELTER study examines the characteristics of diabetic residents in European nursing homes."}{"title": "ISRAEL:Country where a study on the prevalence and characteristics of malnutrition among community-dwelling older adults was conducted."}{"title": "THE NETHERLANDS:Country where the annual national prevalence measurement of care problems related to malnutrition was conducted."}{"title": "ENTERAL NUTRITION:Enteral nutrition is a method of delivering nutrition directly to the stomach or intestines, primarily utilized in patients with specific health conditions. This approach leverages the gastrointestinal tract to provide essential nutrients, ensuring that individuals who may be unable to consume food orally still receive adequate nourishment."}{"title": "JULIA AH:Julia AH is a researcher contributing to the analysis of hospital malnutrition in diabetic patients."}{"title": "MERC\u00c8 P:Merc\u00e8 P is a researcher participating in the study of malnutrition prevalence in diabetic patients."}{"title": "ABELARDO GL:Abelardo GL is a researcher involved in the PREDyCES study on hospital malnutrition."}{"title": "KRYSMARU A:Krysmaru A is a researcher contributing to the study of malnutrition in diabetic patients."}{"title": "SEBASTI\u00c1N C:Sebasti\u00e1n C is a researcher involved in the analysis of hospital malnutrition in patients with diabetes mellitus."}{"title": "GAU BR:Gau BR is a researcher studying the impact of nutritional status on treatment outcomes for diabetic foot ulcers."}{"title": "CHEN HY:Chen HY is a researcher contributing to the study of nutritional status in diabetic patients."}{"title": "HUNG SY:Hung SY is a researcher involved in the study of treatment outcomes for patients with limb-threatening diabetic foot ulcers."}{"title": "YANG HM:Yang HM is a researcher studying the impact of nutritional status on diabetic patients."}{"title": "YEH JT:Yeh JT is a researcher contributing to the study of diabetic foot ulcers."}{"title": "HUANG CH:Huang CH is a researcher involved in the study of diabetic foot ulcers."}{"title": "SUN JH:Sun JH is a researcher studying the impact of nutritional status on diabetic patients."}{"title": "HUANG YY:Huang YY is a researcher contributing to the study of treatment outcomes for diabetic foot ulcers."}{"title": "LINDHOLM C:Lindholm C is a researcher involved in the Pan-European Pressure Ulcer Study."}{"title": "STERNE E:Sterner E is a researcher contributing to the study of pressure ulcers and hip fractures."}{"title": "ROMANELLI M:Romanelli M is a researcher involved in the Pan-European Pressure Ulcer Study."}{"title": "PINA E:Pina E is a researcher contributing to the study of risk factors for pressure ulcers."}{"title": "TORRA Y BOU J:Torra y Bou J is a researcher involved in the study of pressure ulcers."}{"title": "HIETANEN H:Hietanen H is a researcher contributing to the Pan-European Pressure Ulcer Study."}{"title": "IIVANAINEN A:Iivanainen A is a researcher involved in the study of pressure ulcers."}{"title": "GUNNINGBERG L:Gunningberg L is a researcher contributing to the study of risk factors for pressure ulcers."}{"title": "HOMMEL A:Hommel A is a researcher involved in the Pan-European Pressure Ulcer Study."}{"title": "KLANG B:Klang B is a researcher contributing to the study of pressure ulcers."}{"title": "DEALEY C:Dealey C is a researcher involved in the study of pressure ulcers."}{"title": "COX J:Cox J is a researcher reviewing literature on pressure injury risk factors in critical care patients."}{"title": "LIU P:Liu P is a researcher conducting a meta-analysis on diabetes mellitus as a risk factor for pressure ulcers."}{"title": "HE W:He W is a researcher contributing to the study of diabetes mellitus and pressure ulcers."}{"title": "CHEN HL:Chen HL is a researcher involved in the study of diabetes mellitus and surgery-related pressure ulcers."}{"title": "CASIMIRO C:Casimiro C is a researcher involved in the study of nutritional status in elderly patients with diabetes."}{"title": "GARC\u00cdA DE LORENZO A:Garc\u00eda de Lorenzo A is a researcher contributing to the study of dietetic evaluation in elderly patients."}{"title": "US\u00c1N L:Us\u00e1n L is a researcher involved in the study of nutritional status in institutionalized elderly patients."}{"title": "VISCHER UM:Vischer UM is a researcher studying the prevalence of malnutrition in elderly diabetic patients."}{"title": "PERRENOUD L:Perrenoud L is a researcher contributing to the study of malnutrition in elderly patients."}{"title": "GENET C:Genet C is a researcher involved in the study of malnutrition in elderly diabetic patients."}{"title": "ARDIGO S:Ardigo S is a researcher contributing to the study of malnutrition in elderly patients."}{"title": "REGISTE-RAMEAU Y:Registe-Rameau Y is a researcher involved in the study of malnutrition in elderly patients."}{"title": "HERRMANN FR:Herrmann FR is a researcher contributing to the study of malnutrition in elderly diabetic patients."}{"title": "SHARMAN MOSER S:Sharman Moser S is a researcher studying malnutrition among community-dwelling older adults in Israel."}{"title": "MEIJERS JM:Meijers JM is a researcher involved in the national prevalence measurement of care problems in The Netherlands."}{"title": "SCHOLS JM:Schols JM is a researcher contributing to the study of malnutrition prevalence in The Netherlands."}{"title": "VAN BOKHORST-DE VAN DER SCHUEREN MA:Van Bokhorst-de van der Schueren MA is a researcher involved in the study of malnutrition in The Netherlands."}{"title": "DASSEN T:Dassen T is a researcher contributing to the study of malnutrition prevalence in The Netherlands."}{"title": "JANSSEN MA:Janssen MA is a researcher involved in the national prevalence measurement of care problems in The Netherlands."}{"title": "HALFENS RJ:Halfens RJ is a researcher contributing to the study of malnutrition prevalence in The Netherlands."}{"title": "AHMED N:Ahmed N is a researcher studying the impact of malnutrition on survival in Medicare beneficiaries with diabetes."}{"title": "CHOE Y:Choe Y is a researcher involved in the study of malnutrition in Medicare beneficiaries."}{"title": "MUSTAD VA:Mustad VA is a researcher contributing to the study of malnutrition in Medicare beneficiaries."}{"title": "OLIVEIRA FUSTER G:Oliveira Fuster G is a researcher studying dietary-therapeutic product supply in a university hospital."}{"title": "GARC\u00cdA GARC\u00cdA-DONCEL L:Garc\u00eda Garc\u00eda-Doncel L is a researcher involved in the study of dietary-therapeutic products."}{"title": "CARRAL SANLAUREANO F:Carral SanLaureano F is a researcher contributing to the study of dietary-therapeutic products."}{"title": "DOMENECH CIENFUEGOS I:Domenech Cienfuegos I is a researcher involved in the study of dietary-therapeutic products."}{"title": "ARENCIBIA RIVERO T:Arencibia Rivero T is a researcher contributing to the study of dietary-therapeutic products."}{"title": "MANZANO MART\u00cdN MV:Manzano Mart\u00edn MV is a researcher involved in the study of dietary-therapeutic products."}{"title": "PANCOBO-HIDALGO PL:Pancorbo-Hidalgo PL is a researcher studying complications associated with enteral nutrition."}{"title": "GARIN GROUP ANDALUSIAN GROUP FOR NUTRITION REFLECTION AND INVESTIGATION:The GARIN Group is an organization focused on nutrition research and recommendations for managing patients with diabetes or stress hyperglycemia and artificial nutrition."}{"title": "FRANCISCO VILLAZ\u00d3N GONZ\u00c1LEZ:Dr. Francisco Villaz\u00f3n Gonz\u00e1lez is a medical specialist in endocrinology and nutrition, contributing to the understanding of diabetes mellitus in Spain."}{"title": "CIBERDEM:CIBERDEM, officially known as the Centro de Investigaci\u00f3n Biom\u00e9dica en Red de Diabetes y Enfermedades Metab\u00f3licas Asociadas, is a prominent biomedical research center dedicated to the study of diabetes and associated metabolic diseases. This center has conducted significant research, including a study on the incidence of diabetes in Spain, highlighting its commitment to understanding and addressing the challenges posed by these health issues. CIBERDEM plays a crucial role in advancing knowledge and developing solutions related to diabetes and its related conditions."}{"title": "DARIOS STUDY:The DARIOS study is a research project that reviewed multiple studies on cardiovascular risk factors in Spain, revealing a diabetes prevalence of 13%."}{"title": "DI@BET STUDY:The Di@bet study was conducted between 2008 and 2010, assessing diabetes prevalence among the Spanish population, finding a 13.8% prevalence rate."}{"title": "OVIEDO:Oviedo is the capital city of the province of Asturias in Spain, where the Hospital Universitario Central de Asturias is located."}{"title": "DIABETES MELLITUS TYPE 2:"}{"title": "ESPA\u00d1A:Spain is a country that faces significant health challenges, particularly concerning its youth. Nearly 30,000 minors under the age of 15 are affected by Diabetes Mellitus Type 1. Additionally, Spain has reported notable prevalence rates of eating disorders among its population. The country has also been the focus of studies on diabetes incidence, which have revealed alarming prevalence rates, highlighting the urgent need for attention to these health issues."}{"title": "SECCAID:SECCAID is a study that assessed the direct annual costs of diabetes in Spain."}{"title": "HYPERTENSION ARTERIAL:Hypertension is a risk factor associated with diabetes that increases the risk of cardiovascular diseases."}{"title": "DISLIPEMIA:Dyslipidemia is a medical condition characterized by abnormal lipid levels in the blood, which is part of the patient's medical history. This condition affects the patient's lipid levels and is recognized as a significant risk factor associated with diabetes, contributing to potential cardiovascular complications."}{"title": "CANARIAS:Canarias is a region in Spain noted for having higher mortality rates related to diabetes."}{"title": "SISTEMAS DE SALUD:Health systems in Spain are responsible for managing diabetes care and prevention, impacting public health budgets."}{"title": "ENFERMEDADES CARDIOVASCULARES:Cardiovascular diseases are major complications associated with diabetes, increasing mortality risk."}{"title": "PROVINCIA:Provinces in Spain show varying mortality rates related to diabetes, with some regions experiencing higher rates."}{"title": "JUAN FRANCISCO MERINO TORRES:Dr. Juan Francisco Merino Torres is the head of the Endocrinology and Nutrition Service at Hospital Universitario y Polit\u00e9cnico La Fe in Valencia."}{"title": "COMUNIDAD VALENCIANA:The Comunidad Valenciana is an autonomous community located in Spain. It is notable for being the site of a study on diabetes prevalence, which revealed a significant prevalence rate of 14%. This region is characterized by its unique cultural and geographical features, contributing to its identity within Spain."}{"title": "ESTUDIO DI@BET.ES:A study that shows a diabetes prevalence of 13.8% in the population, with a significant portion undiagnosed."}{"title": "COSTE DE LA DIABETES:COSTE DE LA DIABETES refers to the economic impact and healthcare costs associated with diabetes management and treatment. The economic cost of diabetes and its interventions is significant, estimated to reach 11.6% of global health expenditure. This issue is particularly notable in Spain, where the financial burden of diabetes is felt acutely, highlighting the importance of addressing the economic implications of this chronic condition."}{"title": "PREVALENCIA DE DIABETES:The prevalence of diabetes in the adult population in Spain is reported to be 13.8%, with a higher rate among older adults."}{"title": "DEPARTAMENTO DE SALUD LA FE:The Departamento de Salud La Fe is a health department in the Comunidad Valenciana that focuses on diabetes management and health interventions."}{"title": "MEDICINA DE PRECISI\u00d3N:Medicina de Precisi\u00f3n refers to a modern approach in healthcare that tailors medical treatment to the individual characteristics of each patient."}{"title": "BIG DATA:Big Data refers to the large volumes of data that can be analyzed to improve health interventions and patient care."}{"title": "SIP (SISTEMA D'INFORMACI\u00d3 POPULACIONAL):SIP is the identification system used in the Comunidad Valenciana to manage health data."}{"title": "ALCOI:Alcoi is a municipality in the Comunidad Valenciana that is part of the diabetes management program."}{"title": "ALICANTE-HOSPITAL GENERAL:Alicante-Hospital General is a general hospital situated in Alicante, Spain, and is an integral part of the health system in the Comunidad Valenciana. This healthcare facility serves the local population by offering a wide range of medical services, ensuring access to essential healthcare for the community."}{"title": "ALICANTE-SANT JOAN D'ALACANT:Alicante-Sant Joan d'Alacant is a healthcare facility located in the Alicante region of the Comunidad Valenciana. It provides a range of medical services, with a particular focus on diabetes care, among other healthcare offerings."}{"title": "PLATAFORMA TIC EN SALUD:The Plataforma TIC en Salud is a technological platform developed for health data analysis and management in the Comunidad Valenciana."}{"title": "ANATOM\u00cdA PATOL\u00d3GICA:Anatom\u00eda Patol\u00f3gica refers to the study of diseases through the examination of tissues, playing a crucial role in the analysis of health data. This field encompasses the investigation of various pathological conditions, including the confirmation of specific diagnoses. For instance, a recent pathological anatomy report confirmed the diagnosis of neoplasia intraductal papilar mucinosa, highlighting the importance of Anatom\u00eda Patol\u00f3gica in understanding and diagnosing diseases."}{"title": "RADIOLOG\u00cdA:Radiolog\u00eda involves imaging techniques used to diagnose and monitor diseases, including diabetes-related complications."}{"title": "LABORATORIO:Laboratorio refers to medical laboratories that conduct tests and analyses related to health conditions, including diabetes."}{"title": "ATENCI\u00d3N PRIMARIA:Atenci\u00f3n Primaria refers to primary healthcare services that provide initial care and management for patients, including those with diabetes."}{"title": "INTERVENCIONES EN SALUD:Intervenciones en Salud refers to health interventions aimed at preventing and managing diseases like diabetes."}{"title": "OBESIDAD:Obesidad, or obesity, is a chronic condition characterized by an excess accumulation of body fat, which significantly increases the risk of developing diabetes. It complicates nutritional assessment and is associated with a certain degree of inflammation. Due to its health implications, obesity is a critical target for preventive interventions aimed at reducing its prevalence and associated health risks."}{"title": "H\u00c1BITOS ALIMENTARIOS:H\u00e1bitos Alimentarios refers to dietary practices that can influence the risk and management of diabetes."}{"title": "ACTIVIDAD F\u00cdSICA:Actividad F\u00edsica refers to physical activity, which is important for preventing and managing diabetes."}{"title": "ALICANTE (DEPARTAMENTO):Alicante (Departamento) refers to the administrative region in Spain that includes the city of Alicante and its surrounding areas."}{"title": "CASTELLON:Castellon is a province in the Valencian Community of Spain, located to the north of Alicante."}{"title": "VALENCIA-HOSPITAL GENERAL:Valencia-Hospital General is a major hospital in Valencia, providing comprehensive healthcare services."}{"title": "VALENCIA-LA FE:Valencia-La Fe is a prominent hospital in Valencia known for its advanced medical care and research."}{"title": "MANISES:Manises is a municipality in the province of Valencia, Spain, known for its historical significance and proximity to Valencia city."}{"title": "VALENCIA-DOCTOR PESET:Valencia-Doctor Peset is a hospital in Valencia that offers a range of medical services to the community."}{"title": "ELDA:Elda is a city in the province of Alicante, Spain, known for its shoe industry and cultural heritage."}{"title": "VALENCIA (DEPARTAMENTO):"}{"title": "CRIBADO DE DIABETES:Cribado de diabetes refers to the screening process for diabetes in the population, with a reported percentage of 74.35% in the figure."}{"title": "ENFERMEDAD CARDIOVASCULAR:Enfermedad cardiovascular refers to a group of disorders of the heart and blood vessels, which is of particular concern for patients with diabetes."}{"title": "ENFERMEDAD RENAL:Enfermedad renal refers to kidney disease, which can be a complication for patients suffering from diabetes."}{"title": "INERCIA TERAP\u00c9UTICA:Inercia terap\u00e9utica refers to the therapeutic inertia in diabetes treatment, highlighting the delay in prescribing optimal treatments for patients."}{"title": "EMPA-REG STUDY:The EMPA-REG Study is a clinical trial that investigated the cardiovascular safety of a diabetes medication, influencing treatment guidelines."}{"title": "LEADER STUDY:The LEADER Study is a clinical trial that assessed the cardiovascular outcomes of a diabetes medication, impacting treatment practices."}{"title": "EUROASPIRE V:EUROASPIRE V is a study that evaluates the management of cardiovascular disease and diabetes in Europe, providing insights into treatment practices.)<|COMPLETE|>"}{"title": "MESA REDONDA DE CASOS CL\u00cdNICOS:The \"MESA REDONDA DE CASOS CL\u00cdNICOS\" is a round table event focused on discussing clinical cases within the medical community. It features various medical professionals who present and analyze different cases. The event has taken place in the Comunidad Valenciana, where a diverse group of specialists share their insights. Additionally, there is a specific iteration of this event that addresses clinical cases related to diabetes and nutrition, which was held in Granada, also involving various specialists. Overall, the MESA REDONDA DE CASOS CL\u00cdNICOS serves as a platform for collaboration and knowledge exchange among healthcare professionals across different regions and specialties."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME MELAS:A rare genetic disorder discussed in one of the clinical cases, characterized by mitochondrial dysfunction and associated with diabetes."}{"title": "OBESIDAD M\u00d3RBIDA:\"OBESIDAD M\u00d3RBIDA\" refers to a medical condition characterized by severe obesity, which poses significant health risks and complications. This condition has been discussed in clinical cases, highlighting its impact on patients who often experience multiple attempts at weight loss and may ultimately require surgical intervention, such as bariatric surgery. Morbid obesity is particularly resistant to conventional treatment methods and is associated with an increased risk of serious health issues, including diabetes and pancreatic cancer. Overall, \"obesidad m\u00f3rbida\" represents a critical health concern that necessitates comprehensive management and intervention strategies."}{"title": "NEOPLASIA INTRADUCTAL PAPILAR MUCINOSA:Neoplasia intraductal papilar mucinosa is a specific type of pancreatic tumor that has been discussed in clinical cases. It is associated with malnutrition and diabetes, highlighting its potential impact on the patient's overall health. The patient in the case was diagnosed with this type of tumor, indicating its clinical significance and the need for careful management of related health issues."}{"title": "HOSPITAL GENERAL UNIVERSITARIO SANTA LUC\u00cdA:Hospital General Universitario Santa Luc\u00eda is a healthcare institution in Cartagena where specialized medical care is provided, including for patients with endocrine and nutritional needs."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME DE MELAS:MELAS is a mitochondrial disease characterized by encephalomyopathy, lactic acidosis, and stroke-like episodes, significantly affecting muscle and nervous system function, often leading to complications such as diabetes mellitus."}{"title": "CIRUG\u00cdA BARI\u00c1TRICA:CIRUG\u00cdA BARI\u00c1TRICA refers to a medical procedure increasingly utilized to address obesity, particularly among diabetic patients. This surgical intervention is designed to assist individuals suffering from obesity in losing weight and managing associated health complications, including type 2 diabetes. Specifically, bariatric surgery is often performed as an elective procedure for patients with morbid obesity, with one common method being a simplified gastric bypass. While the procedure is associated with low complication rates, it is important to note that the risks may increase with additional interventions. Overall, CIRUG\u00cdA BARI\u00c1TRICA serves as a significant option for improving health outcomes in individuals struggling with severe obesity."}{"title": "ENFERMEDADES MITOCONDRIALES:Mitochondrial diseases are a group of disorders caused by dysfunctional mitochondria, which can lead to a variety of health issues, including metabolic and neurological problems."}{"title": "MALNUTRICI\u00d3N CAL\u00d3RICA SEVERA:Severe caloric malnutrition is a condition resulting from inadequate intake of calories, leading to significant health issues, particularly in patients with complex medical conditions like MELAS."}{"title": "POLINEUROPAT\u00cdA SENSITIVO-MOTORA:POLINEUROPAT\u00cdA SENSITIVO-MOTORA, also known as sensory-motor polyneuropathy, is a medical condition that impacts the peripheral nerves. This condition is characterized by both sensory loss and motor weakness, which can significantly affect a patient's quality of life. It is often observed in individuals with mitochondrial diseases, highlighting a potential link between these two health issues. Overall, sensory-motor polyneuropathy represents a serious neurological disorder that requires careful management and treatment."}{"title": "DUODENOPANCREATECTOM\u00cdA:Duodenopancreatectomy is a surgical procedure involving the removal of the duodenum and pancreas, often performed in cases of pancreatic cancer, which can lead to complications such as diabetes and malabsorption."}{"title": "CARCINOMA MUCINOSO DE P\u00c1NCREAS:Mucinous pancreatic carcinoma is a type of cancer that affects the pancreas, characterized by the production of mucin, and may require surgical intervention like duodenopancreatectomy."}{"title": "MELAS:MELAS, which stands for Mitochondrial Encephalomyopathy, Lactic Acidosis, and Stroke-like episodes, is the most common mitochondrial disease. It is characterized by a heterogeneous phenotypic expression that includes a variety of symptoms affecting multiple systems in the body. Individuals with MELAS often experience neurological impairments, such as migraines, seizures, and episodes resembling strokes. Additionally, the disorder can lead to muscular weakness and various gastrointestinal issues, which frequently result in malnutrition. Other systemic manifestations may include diabetes mellitus. The complexity of MELAS symptoms can vary significantly among affected individuals, making diagnosis and management challenging. One patient was diagnosed with MELAS in 2008, highlighting the ongoing recognition and understanding of this condition."}{"title": "ARGININA:Arginina is an amino acid that plays a crucial role in the production of nitric oxide (NO), a compound essential for vascular relaxation. It is considered a therapeutic agent that may enhance the availability of nitric oxide, potentially aiding in the treatment of symptoms associated with MELAS (Mitochondrial Encephalomyopathy, Lactic Acidosis, and Stroke-like episodes). Through its involvement in nitric oxide synthesis, Arginina is linked to the underlying pathology of MELAS, suggesting its importance in managing this condition."}{"title": "CITRULINA:Citrulina is an amino acid supplement known for its role in increasing the production of nitric oxide (NO) in the body. It is considered to have better absorption and bioavailability compared to arginine, another amino acid. While Citrulina is relevant in the context of MELAS (Mitochondrial Encephalomyopathy, Lactic Acidosis, and Stroke-like episodes), particularly for patients who exhibit low levels of nitric oxide, its specific effects on this condition have not been thoroughly studied."}{"title": "CITOCROMO C:Citocromo C is an enzyme that has a high affinity for nitric oxide and is implicated in the pathophysiology of MELAS due to its interaction with nitric oxide synthase."}{"title": "ACIDOSIS L\u00c1CTICA:Acidosis l\u00e1ctica is a prevalent condition observed in patients with MELAS (Mitochondrial Encephalomyopathy, Lactic Acidosis, and Stroke-like episodes). It arises due to mitochondrial dysfunction, which is a hallmark of the syndrome. This metabolic disturbance is characterized by an accumulation of lactic acid in the body, and it is recognized as a diagnostic criterion for MELAS."}{"title": "EPILESIA:Epilepsy is a neurological manifestation observed in a significant percentage of MELAS patients, contributing to the overall clinical picture of the syndrome."}{"title": "NEUROPAT\u00cdA PERIF\u00c9RICA:Neuropat\u00eda perif\u00e9rica is a condition affecting the peripheral nerves, noted in MELAS patients, contributing to their neurological symptoms."}{"title": "\u00d3XIDO N\u00cdTRICO:\u00d3xido n\u00edtrico is a signaling molecule that plays a critical role in vascular relaxation and is implicated in the pathophysiology of MELAS due to its interaction with endothelial cells."}{"title": "CITOCROMO C OXIDASA:Citocromo C oxidasa is an enzyme that is involved in the electron transport chain and is noted for its increased activity in MELAS patients, affecting nitric oxide availability."}{"title": "HIPOACUSIA NEUROSENSORIAL:Hipoacusia neurosensorial is a type of hearing loss that is commonly observed in patients with MELAS (Mitochondrial Encephalomyopathy, Lactic Acidosis, and Stroke-like episodes). This auditory manifestation significantly contributes to the overall neurological symptoms associated with the syndrome, thereby affecting the quality of life of those affected. Additionally, it is noted that hipoacusia neurosensorial can also be experienced by family members, such as the patient's mother, indicating a potential genetic link related to the underlying mutation."}{"title": "DEMANDA DE INSULINA:Demanda de insulina refers to the requirement for insulin treatment in MELAS patients, particularly in those developing diabetes mellitus."}{"title": "NEW CASTLE:New Castle is associated with the scale of severity for adult mitochondrial diseases, specifically the NMDAS used to assess patients with MELAS."}{"title": "COENZIMA Q10:Coenzima Q10 is a compound that stabilizes the electron transport chain and has antioxidant properties, potentially benefiting patients with MELAS."}{"title": "IMC:The \u00cdndice de Masa Corporal (IMC), or Body Mass Index (BMI), is a critical measure used to assess body weight in relation to height, which is essential for evaluating the nutritional status of individuals. It serves as a tool for classifying obesity and identifying malnutrition risks. For instance, one patient exhibited an IMC of 16 kg/m\u00b2, indicating a low weight for their height of 1.75 m, while another patient had an IMC of 36.2 kg/m\u00b2 at discharge and a subsequent IMC of 29.44 kg/m\u00b2 during a follow-up review, reflecting a significant change in their nutritional status over time. Generally, an IMC value below 20 kg/m\u00b2 is associated with a risk of malnutrition, highlighting the importance of monitoring this index in clinical settings. Overall, the IMC is a vital metric for understanding and managing patients' health concerning their weight and height."}{"title": "S\u00cdNTOMAS GASTROINTESTINALES:S\u00edntomas gastrointestinales refer to digestive symptoms that increase the risk of malnutrition in patients with MELAS."}{"title": "DIETA CETOG\u00c9NICA:Dieta cetog\u00e9nica is a dietary approach that may reduce epileptic seizures in MELAS patients, although its long-term safety and effectiveness are unknown."}{"title": "EPILEPSIA:Epilepsia is a neurological manifestation that occurs in a significant percentage of MELAS patients, contributing to their overall health challenges."}{"title": "DEMANCIAS PSIQUI\u00c1TRICAS:Demanias psiqui\u00e1tricas refer to psychiatric manifestations that may arise in patients with MELAS, impacting their mental health."}{"title": "MIOTOP\u00cdA:Miopat\u00eda is a cardinal manifestation of MELAS, characterized by muscle weakness and intolerance to exercise."}{"title": "MIOCARDIOPAT\u00cdA HIPERTR\u00d3FICA:Miocardiopat\u00eda hipertr\u00f3fica is a cardiac manifestation that can occur in MELAS patients, affecting heart function."}{"title": "TALLA BAJA:Talla baja refers to short stature, which can be a manifestation in MELAS patients due to hormonal deficiencies."}{"title": "FALLO DE MEDRO:Fallo de medro is a condition of poor growth that can occur in MELAS patients, often linked to nutritional issues."}{"title": "PACIENTES:"}{"title": "ARGININE:Arginine is an amino acid used in the patient's chronic treatment to manage symptoms associated with MELAS."}{"title": "L-CARNITINE:L-Carnitine is a supplement that plays a crucial role in fatty acid metabolism and is included in treatment regimens to potentially enhance mitochondrial function. It is particularly suggested for patients with primary systemic carnitine deficiency, where it is recognized for its safety and effectiveness in correcting underlying carnitine deficits."}{"title": "COENZYME Q10:Coenzyme Q10 is a compound involved in energy production in cells, used in the patient's treatment to address complications related to MELAS."}{"title": "CLOPIDOGREL:Clopidogrel is a medication used in the patient's treatment, likely for its antiplatelet effects."}{"title": "LACOSAMIDE:Lacosamide is an anticonvulsant medication included in the patient's treatment to manage seizures."}{"title": "RANITIDINE:Ranitidine is a medication used to reduce stomach acid, prescribed to the patient for gastrointestinal symptoms."}{"title": "LEVETIRACETAM:Levetiracetam is an anticonvulsant medication used in the patient's treatment to control seizures."}{"title": "LAMOTRIGINE:Lamotrigine is an anticonvulsant medication included in the patient's treatment plan for seizure management."}{"title": "DOMPERIDONE:Domperidone is a medication used to relieve nausea and vomiting, prescribed to the patient to manage gastrointestinal symptoms."}{"title": "LACTITOL:Lactitol is a laxative used in the patient's treatment to manage constipation."}{"title": "MOTHER:The mother of the patient is a carrier of the A243G mutation and has her own health issues, including diabetes and hearing loss."}{"title": "PATIENT:The patient encompasses a diverse group of individuals with varying health conditions. One notable case is a 29-year-old woman diagnosed with MELAS (Mitochondrial Encephalomyopathy, Lactic Acidosis, and Stroke-like episodes), who is experiencing multiple neurological and gastrointestinal symptoms, necessitating chronic treatment. Additionally, there is a 76-year-old male patient suffering from type 2 diabetes and moderate to severe malnutrition, who requires specialized nutritional support and careful monitoring. Furthermore, the patient is also described as an individual undergoing nutritional assessment and treatment specifically for diabetes and malnutrition. Lastly, another aspect of the patient includes an individual with an oncological condition, specifically a neuroendocrine tumor of the pancreas, who requires various types of nutritional support throughout their treatment. Collectively, these descriptions highlight the complex and multifaceted health needs of patients dealing with chronic illnesses, nutritional deficiencies, and oncological conditions."}{"title": "CRISIS CONVULSIVAS:Crisis convulsivas refers to the repeated generalized seizures experienced by the patient."}{"title": "NAUSEAS:Nauseas are gastrointestinal symptoms experienced by the patient, contributing to her overall health issues."}{"title": "VOMITOS:V\u00f3mitos are episodes of vomiting that the patient has experienced, affecting her treatment compliance."}{"title": "ESTRE\u00d1IMIENTO:Estre\u00f1imiento refers to the constipation issues faced by the patient, which are part of her gastrointestinal symptoms."}{"title": "HIPERPROLACTINEMIA:Hiperprolactinemia is a condition of elevated prolactin levels that the patient's mother has, associated with her health issues."}{"title": "MICROADENOMA HIPOFISARIO:Microadenoma hipofisario is a small tumor on the pituitary gland that the patient's mother had, resolved with treatment."}{"title": "BAJA TALLA:Baja talla refers to the short stature experienced by the patient during childhood, part of her endocrine issues."}{"title": "DIFICULTADES EN LAS ACTIVIDADES BASALES:Dificultades en las actividades basales refers to the patient's dependency for daily living activities due to her health condition."}{"title": "GASTRITIS ATR\u00d3FICA:Gastritis atr\u00f3fica is a condition diagnosed in the patient, indicating inflammation of the stomach lining."}{"title": "POLIPOS MULTIPLES:P\u00f3lipos m\u00faltiples are growths found in the patient's gastrointestinal tract, contributing to her digestive issues."}{"title": "ELECTROLITOS ANORMALES:Electrolitos anormales refers to abnormal electrolyte levels found in the patient's clinical tests."}{"title": "MUTACI\u00d3N A243G:Mutaci\u00f3n A243G is a genetic mutation associated with the patient's mother's health issues and the patient's MELAS diagnosis.)<|COMPLETE|>"}{"title": "SNG:SNG, or nasogastric tube, is a medical device utilized for feeding and medication administration in patients who have difficulties swallowing or cannot safely consume food orally. It serves as a method of nutritional support, specifically designed for enteral feeding. The nasogastric tube is essential for providing nutrition to patients who require assistance due to various medical conditions. In Spanish, SNG is referred to as \"sonda nasog\u00e1strica,\" emphasizing its role in enteral nutrition for patients. Overall, SNG is a critical tool in the management of patients needing dietary support through alternative means."}{"title": "HOSPITALIZACI\u00d3N:Hospitalizaci\u00f3n refers to the process of admitting a patient to a hospital for medical treatment. This may be necessary for various conditions, including head and neck cancers, where patients may require a period of hospitalization for their treatment. Additionally, hospitalizaci\u00f3n can also be essential in cases such as acute pancreatitis, where patients need specialized care. Furthermore, the hospitalization process may involve monitoring and treating severe malnutrition and its related complications, ensuring that patients receive comprehensive medical attention during their stay."}{"title": "CLOSTRIDIUM DIFFICILE:Clostridium difficile is a bacterium that the patient was tested for due to gastrointestinal symptoms."}{"title": "P\u00c9PTIDO C:Peptide C is a marker measured in the patient's study to assess insulin production."}{"title": "INSULINA:Insulina is a crucial hormone used in the management of diabetes, particularly Type 1 diabetes. It plays a vital role in regulating blood glucose levels, which is essential for the health of patients, including those with additional conditions such as pancreatic cancer. The patient has been receiving insulin treatment as part of their diabetes management, with adjustments made to both basal and corrective insulin guidelines to optimize their blood sugar control. \n\nDespite the importance of insulin therapy, the patient has been omitting doses, which can adversely affect their blood sugar management. Insulin levels have been closely monitored and adjusted following the patient's diabetes diagnosis to ensure effective treatment. The administration of insulin is tailored to the patient's needs, with different regimens employed to maintain stable glucose levels. Overall, insulina is integral to the patient's treatment plan, influencing not only their diabetes management but also their overall nutritional status and health."}{"title": "GLUCEMIA:GLUCEMIA refers to the concentration of glucose in the blood, which is a crucial factor in managing diabetes. Blood glucose levels were regularly monitored during the patient's treatment for diabetes and malnutrition, highlighting the importance of tracking these levels for effective management. In particular, glucemia is significant in the context of diabetes management, as it is influenced by dietary intake and can vary based on individual health conditions. This is especially relevant for patients with specific syndromes, such as MELAS syndrome, where blood sugar levels play a key role in overall health. Notably, the patient's blood sugar levels were critically high during her re-admission in May 2016, underscoring the need for careful monitoring and management of glucemia in diabetic patients."}{"title": "TABLA 4:Table 4 contains laboratory results during the patient's hospitalization, detailing various blood parameters."}{"title": "TABLA 5:Table 5 presents the results of the study conducted to assess the patient's hyperglycemic syndrome."}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N:NUTRICI\u00d3N encompasses the essential dietary management and support provided to patients, particularly those facing significant health challenges such as cancer and diabetes. It plays a vital role in preventing conditions like cachexia, improving the quality of life for cancer patients, and is a critical focus in the management of diabetes. Nutritional assessment and intervention are crucial for recovery, especially following surgery, and are integral to addressing specific health conditions. For patients with MNGIE, nutritional support becomes even more important, particularly for those experiencing substantial weight loss and gastrointestinal issues. Overall, NUTRICI\u00d3N is dedicated to offering comprehensive dietary assistance to patients, particularly in cases of malnutrition and other related health concerns."}{"title": "GASTROSTOM\u00cdA ENDOSC\u00d3PICA PERCUT\u00c1NEA:Gastrostomy is a procedure performed to provide nutritional support through a PEG for patients unable to eat normally."}{"title": "INSULINA GLARGINA:Insulina Glargina is a long-acting insulin utilized by patients for the management of diabetes. It is administered at night and is specifically designed to help control blood sugar levels effectively. This insulin plays a crucial role in managing blood glucose levels in diabetic patients, including those with type 2 diabetes. Additionally, Insulina Glargina is noted for its use in managing diabetes post-surgery and is also mentioned in the context of nutritional therapy for patients with Alzheimer's disease. Overall, Insulina Glargina serves as an essential medication for maintaining optimal blood sugar control in various patient scenarios."}{"title": "F\u00d3RMULA ESPEC\u00cdFICA PARA DIABETES:A specialized formula designed for diabetic patients to help manage their blood glucose levels effectively."}{"title": "TABLA 6:Table 6 presents the complementary tests results six months after the initiation of artificial nutritional support, indicating various health parameters of the patient."}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N ENTERAL SUPLEMENTARIA:Enteral nutrition is a method of delivering nutrients directly into the gastrointestinal tract, used in this case to support the patient's dietary needs."}{"title": "FIGURA 1:"}{"title": "MELAS SYNDROME:MELAS syndrome is a mitochondrial disorder characterized by mitochondrial encephalopathy, lactic acidosis, and stroke-like episodes, often leading to complications such as diabetes and other health issues."}{"title": "PEG:PEG, or percutaneous endoscopic gastrostomy, is a medical procedure designed to facilitate nutrition for patients who are unable to adequately feed themselves orally. This method provides long-term nutritional support and is particularly useful in managing the nutritional needs of patients with specific medical conditions, such as diabetes and MELAS syndrome. The procedure involves the placement of a feeding tube directly into the stomach through the abdominal wall, allowing for enteral nutrition to be administered effectively."}{"title": "THORBURN DR:Thorburn DR is an author who has contributed to the understanding of mitochondrial disorders, including MELAS syndrome."}{"title": "RAHMAN S:Rahman S is a researcher who has studied genetic mutations related to mitochondrial disorders and their implications."}{"title": "PIA S:Pia S is an author who has written about MELAS syndrome and its clinical implications."}{"title": "NIEDERMAYR K:Niedermayr K is a researcher who has explored mitochondrial DNA mutations and their clinical presentations."}{"title": "IKEDA T:Ikeda T is a researcher who has studied mitochondrial DNA mutations in patients with MELAS syndrome."}{"title": "WANG XL:Wang XL is a researcher who has investigated the relationship between genetic polymorphisms and coronary artery disease."}{"title": "VOS MH:Vos MH is a researcher who has studied the dynamics of nitric oxide in mitochondrial function."}{"title": "KOGA Y:Koga Y is a researcher who has examined endothelial dysfunction in MELAS syndrome and its treatment options."}{"title": "NAINI A:Naini A is a researcher who has studied hypocitrullinemia in patients with MELAS syndrome."}{"title": "EL-HATTAB AW:El-Hattab AW is a researcher who has explored clinical manifestations and treatment options for MELAS syndrome."}{"title": "AL-GADI IS:Al-Gadi IS is a researcher who has studied endocrine disorders in primary mitochondrial disease."}{"title": "WHITTAKER RG:Whittaker RG is a researcher who has investigated the prevalence and progression of diabetes in mitochondrial disease."}{"title": "SCHAEFER AM:Schaefer AM is a researcher who has studied endocrine disorders in mitochondrial disease."}{"title": "SPROULE DM:Sproule DM is a researcher who has written about the clinical phenotype and management of MELAS syndrome."}{"title": "NESBITT V:Nesbitt V is a researcher involved in the UK MRC Mitochondrial Disease Patient Cohort Study."}{"title": "DE LAAT P:De Laat P is a researcher who has studied dysphagia and gastrointestinal problems in patients with mitochondrial disease."}{"title": "NUTRITIONAL STATUS:Nutritional status refers to the condition of a person's health as it relates to the intake and utilization of nutrients. It encompasses the overall state of the body in relation to these nutrients, which is essential for maintaining health and managing various medical conditions, including MELAS syndrome. Understanding nutritional status is crucial for ensuring that individuals receive the necessary nutrients for optimal health and effective management of specific health issues."}{"title": "GENETIC MUTATION:Genetic mutations are alterations in the DNA sequence that can lead to various disorders, including those affecting mitochondrial function, such as MELAS syndrome."}{"title": "ENDOCRINE DISORDERS:Endocrine disorders are conditions that affect the endocrine system, which can be associated with mitochondrial diseases like MELAS syndrome."}{"title": "LACTIC ACIDOSIS:Lactic acidosis is a condition characterized by the buildup of lactic acid in the body, often seen in mitochondrial disorders like MELAS syndrome."}{"title": "STROKE-LIKE EPISODES:Stroke-like episodes are neurological events that can occur in patients with MELAS syndrome, leading to various symptoms and complications."}{"title": "MITOCHONDRIAL DNA:Mitochondrial DNA is the DNA located in mitochondria, which can harbor mutations leading to mitochondrial diseases, including MELAS syndrome."}{"title": "CLINICAL PHENOTYPE:Clinical phenotype refers to the observable characteristics and symptoms of a disease, which in the case of MELAS syndrome can vary widely among patients."}{"title": "TREATMENT OPTIONS:Treatment options for MELAS syndrome may include dietary management, exercise, and specific therapies aimed at managing symptoms and complications."}{"title": "DYSFUNCTION:Dysfunction refers to impaired or abnormal functioning, which can occur in various systems of the body in patients with mitochondrial diseases like MELAS syndrome."}{"title": "MITOCHONDRIAL DISORDERS:"}{"title": "MAR\u00cdA JOS\u00c9 MOLINA PUERTA:Mar\u00eda Jos\u00e9 Molina Puerta is a specialist in Endocrinology and Nutrition at Hospital Universitario Reina Sof\u00eda in C\u00f3rdoba."}{"title": "HOSPITAL UNIVERSITARIO REINA SOF\u00cdA:Hospital Universitario Reina Sof\u00eda is a medical institution located in C\u00f3rdoba, specializing in various healthcare services."}{"title": "BYPASS G\u00c1STRICO:Gastric bypass is a type of weight-loss surgery that involves creating a small pouch from the stomach and connecting it directly to the small intestine."}{"title": "DEHISCENCIA DE SUTURA:Suture dehiscence is a complication that occurs when a surgical wound reopens, which can happen postoperatively."}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N ENTERAL TOTAL:NUTRICI\u00d3N ENTERAL TOTAL, also known as total enteral nutrition, is a method of feeding that delivers all nutritional requirements directly through the gastrointestinal tract. This approach was specifically implemented for a patient following bariatric surgery due to complications that arose during the recovery process."}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N PARENTERAL TOTAL:NUTRICI\u00d3N PARENTERAL TOTAL, also known as Total Parenteral Nutrition (TPN), is a treatment designed to deliver nutrients directly into the bloodstream, bypassing the gastrointestinal tract. This method is particularly utilized for patients who are unable to consume food orally. In the case of a specific patient, TPN was initiated following the loss of a nasoenteric tube and prior to the resumption of oral feeding. During the patient's hospitalization, TPN served as a crucial means of providing nutritional support, ensuring that the necessary nutrients were supplied directly into the bloodstream to meet the patient's dietary needs."}{"title": "MUJER DE 48 A\u00d1OS:Una mujer de 48 a\u00f1os que ha sido intervenida de cirug\u00eda bari\u00e1trica y tiene antecedentes de diabetes tipo 2 y obesidad m\u00f3rbida."}{"title": "ENDOCOPIA DIGESTIVA ALTA:Procedimiento m\u00e9dico que fue muy mal tolerado por la paciente durante la evaluaci\u00f3n de su condici\u00f3n."}{"title": "MEDICAMENTOS:Tratamientos habituales de la paciente que incluyen metformina, liraglutida, insulina, losart\u00e1n, atorvastatina, ezetrol y adiro."}{"title": "HIPERLIPEMIA:Condici\u00f3n m\u00e9dica de la paciente que se menciona como parte de sus antecedentes personales."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME DEPRESIVO:Condici\u00f3n m\u00e9dica de la paciente que se menciona como parte de sus antecedentes personales."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME DE APNEA OBSTRUCTIVA DEL SUE\u00d1O:Condici\u00f3n m\u00e9dica de la paciente que est\u00e1 pendiente de confirmaci\u00f3n mediante estudio."}{"title": "MEFORMINA:Medicamento utilizado por la paciente para el control de la diabetes tipo 2."}{"title": "LIRAGLUTIDE:Medicamento utilizado por la paciente, administrado como inyecci\u00f3n para el control de la diabetes tipo 2."}{"title": "LOSART\u00c1N:Medicamento utilizado por la paciente para el tratamiento de la hipertensi\u00f3n arterial."}{"title": "ATORVASTATINA:Atorvastatin is a medication that the patient takes to manage dyslipidemia and lower cholesterol levels. It is utilized by the patient for the control of blood lipids, indicating its role in maintaining healthy cholesterol levels and overall cardiovascular health."}{"title": "EZETROL:Medicamento utilizado por la paciente para el control de l\u00edpidos en sangre."}{"title": "ADIRO:Medicamento utilizado por la paciente como parte de su tratamiento habitual."}{"title": "HIIPERTENSI\u00d3N ARTERIAL:"}{"title": "ENDOSCOPIA DIGESTIVA ALTA:La endoscopia digestiva alta es un procedimiento realizado para evaluar el estado del es\u00f3fago, est\u00f3mago y duodeno de la paciente, que mostr\u00f3 una hernia de hiato y mucosa normal."}{"title": "ENFERMER\u00cdA EDUCADORA:La enfermera educadora es responsable de la educaci\u00f3n nutricional de la paciente antes de la cirug\u00eda bari\u00e1trica."}{"title": "TOMOGRAF\u00cdA AXIAL COMPUTERIZADA:La tomograf\u00eda axial computerizada fue realizada para confirmar la existencia de un trayecto fistuloso en la sutura gastroyeyunal tras la cirug\u00eda."}{"title": "DIETA DIAB\u00c9TICA HIPERPROTEICA:La dieta diab\u00e9tica hiperproteica es el r\u00e9gimen alimenticio que se implement\u00f3 para la paciente durante su recuperaci\u00f3n postoperatoria."}{"title": "F\u00cdSTULA G\u00c1STRICA:La f\u00edstula g\u00e1strica es una complicaci\u00f3n postoperatoria que se sospech\u00f3 en la paciente tras la cirug\u00eda bari\u00e1trica."}{"title": "DRENAJE:El drenaje es un procedimiento que se realiz\u00f3 en la paciente para manejar el d\u00e9bito sucio postoperatorio tras la cirug\u00eda bari\u00e1trica."}{"title": "FEDERACI\u00d3N INTERNACIONAL DE DIABETES:The Federaci\u00f3n Internacional de Diabetes (IDF) is an organization dedicated to establishing guidelines and recommendations for the treatment of diabetes. It plays a crucial role in providing guidance on various aspects of diabetes management, including the consideration of metabolic surgery for patients suffering from morbid obesity. Through its efforts, the IDF aims to improve the care and outcomes for individuals affected by diabetes worldwide."}{"title": "CONTROL GLUC\u00c9MICO:Control gluc\u00e9mico refers to the management and regulation of a patient's blood glucose levels throughout their treatment. It is a crucial aspect of patient care, particularly involving the administration of insulin to effectively manage blood glucose levels. In the context of treatment with NET (Nutritional Enteral Therapy) and NPT (Nutritional Parenteral Therapy), the control gluc\u00e9mico was noted to be adequate, ensuring that the patient's glucose levels were maintained within a desirable range during their treatment."}{"title": "TRATAMIENTO M\u00c9DICO INTENSIVO:El tratamiento m\u00e9dico intensivo se refiere a las intervenciones m\u00e9dicas que se aplican a la paciente para el control de la diabetes tipo 2, complementando la cirug\u00eda bari\u00e1trica."}{"title": "ESTUDIO STAMPEDE:El estudio STAMPEDE es una investigaci\u00f3n que demuestra la efectividad de la cirug\u00eda bari\u00e1trica en el control gluc\u00e9mico en pacientes obesos con diabetes tipo 2."}{"title": "ASOCIACI\u00d3N AMERICANA DE DIABETES:The Asociaci\u00f3n Americana de Diabetes (ADA) provides recommendations for diabetes management, including the possibility of surgery for certain patients."}{"title": "SOCIEDAD ESPA\u00d1OLA PARA EL ESTUDIO DE LA OBESIDAD:The Sociedad Espa\u00f1ola para el Estudio de la Obesidad is a society that provides criteria for evaluating the results of metabolic surgery."}{"title": "SOCIEDAD ESPA\u00d1OLA DE LA CIRUG\u00cdA DE LA ENFERMEDAD M\u00d3RBIDA:The Sociedad Espa\u00f1ola de la Cirug\u00eda de la Enfermedad M\u00f3rbida is a society that collaborates with SEEDO to establish guidelines for metabolic surgery."}{"title": "KUMPF:Kumpf is a researcher whose work reflects the outcomes of patients after metabolic surgery, particularly regarding dietary changes and complications."}{"title": "DOBRATZ:Dobratz is a researcher who evaluated predictive equations for measuring basal metabolic expenditure in obese women."}{"title": "CIRUG\u00cdA METAB\u00d3LICA:Metabolic surgery is a medical procedure recommended for treating type 2 diabetes in patients with obesity."}{"title": "SOPORTE NUTRICIONAL:SOPORTE NUTRICIONAL refers to the provision of dietary assistance to patients who are unable to meet their nutritional needs through normal eating. This type of nutritional support is particularly crucial for patients who have undergone metabolic surgery, especially in cases where complications arise. It serves as a necessary intervention to ensure that these patients receive adequate nutrition during their recovery process."}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N PARENTERAL:NUTRICI\u00d3N PARENTERAL, or parenteral nutrition (NP), is a medical treatment that provides essential nutrients directly into the bloodstream, bypassing the gastrointestinal tract. This method is utilized primarily in patients who are unable to consume food orally or tolerate enteral nutrition, particularly in cases such as pancreatitis or post-surgery recovery. During hospitalization, parenteral nutrition serves as an alternative means of nutritional support, ensuring that patients receive adequate nourishment when traditional feeding methods are not viable or contraindicated. Overall, NUTRICI\u00d3N PARENTERAL is a critical intervention for maintaining the nutritional status of patients who cannot meet their dietary needs through oral or enteral means."}{"title": "FUGA ANASTOM\u00d3TICA:Fuga anastom\u00f3tica is a common complication after metabolic surgery that may require nutritional support due to its impact on oral intake."}{"title": "NA\u00daSEAS Y V\u00d3MITOS:Nauseas y v\u00f3mitos are common post-operative complications that can limit a patient's ability to eat normally after metabolic surgery."}{"title": "MALABSORCI\u00d3N SEVERA:Malabsorci\u00f3n severa is a serious condition that can occur post-surgery, affecting nutrient absorption and necessitating nutritional support."}{"title": "DIETA ORAL:Dieta oral refers to the normal diet that most patients transition to after metabolic surgery, although some may face complications that prevent this."}{"title": "CALORIMETR\u00cdA INDIRECTA:Calorimetr\u00eda indirecta is a method used to measure basal metabolic rate, which is important for determining nutritional needs in post-operative patients."}{"title": "EQUACIONES PREDICTIVAS:Ecuaciones predictivas are formulas used to estimate metabolic expenditure in patients, especially when calorimetry is unavailable.)<|COMPLETE|>"}{"title": "SOCIEDAD AMERICANA DE NUTRICI\u00d3N PARENTERAL Y ENTERAL:ASPEN is an organization that provides guidelines for nutritional support in hospitalized adult obese patients, particularly in the context of bariatric surgery."}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N HIPERPROTEICA:Hyperproteic nutrition is recommended for patients without severe liver or kidney dysfunction, aiming to avoid negative consequences of overfeeding."}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N HIPOCAL\u00d3RICA:Hypocaloric nutrition is designed to prevent negative outcomes associated with overfeeding, such as hyperglycemia and increased infection rates."}{"title": "UNIDAD DE CUIDADOS INTENSIVOS:The Intensive Care Unit (UCI) is a specialized department in hospitals where patients receive close monitoring and care, particularly for nutritional adjustments."}{"title": "NIVEL DE RECOMENDACI\u00d3N BAJO:A low level of recommendation indicates that the evidence supporting a particular nutritional approach is not strong, as seen in the guidelines for nutritional support in bariatric surgery."}{"title": "NIVELES DE CUIDADO:Levels of care refer to the different intensities of medical care provided, particularly in the context of monitoring nutritional intake in critical patients."}{"title": "PAR\u00c1METROS CL\u00cdNICOS:Clinical parameters are metrics used to assess a patient's health status, including wound healing and early mobilization in the context of nutritional support."}{"title": "DEFICIENCIAS NUTRICIONALES:Nutritional deficiencies are conditions that arise when the body does not get enough nutrients, which can be a risk for patients undergoing bariatric surgery."}{"title": "FLUIDOS Y ELECTROLITOS:Fluids and electrolytes are essential for maintaining hydration and electrolyte balance, which must be closely monitored in patients receiving nutritional support."}{"title": "NIVELES DE GLUCEMIA:Blood glucose levels are monitored to manage the metabolic state of patients, particularly those undergoing bariatric surgery.)<|COMPLETE|>"}{"title": "HOSPITAL GENERAL UNIVERSITARIO MORALES MESEGUER:Hospital General Universitario Morales Meseguer is a healthcare institution located in Murcia, specializing in various medical fields including endocrinology and nutrition."}{"title": "YAMINA SULEIMAN MARTOS:Dra. Yamina Suleiman Martos is a specialist in endocrinology and nutrition, involved in the clinical management of diabetes and related conditions."}{"title": "MURCIA:Murcia is a region in Spain where the Hospital General Universitario Morales Meseguer is located."}{"title": "MNGIE:MNGIE, or mitochondrial neurogastrointestinal encephalomyopathy, is a rare genetic disorder characterized by a deficiency in thymidine phosphorylase, which is caused by mutations in the TYMP gene. This disorder primarily affects the gastrointestinal and nervous systems, resulting in a range of metabolic issues and complications, including diabetes. Due to the complexity of the symptoms and the interplay between the affected systems, MNGIE requires intricate treatment approaches to manage its severe manifestations."}{"title": "NUTRICIONAL SUPPLEMENTS:Nutritional supplements are products taken to enhance dietary intake, often used in clinical settings to support patients with specific health conditions."}{"title": "FENOFIBRATO:Fenofibrate is a medication used to reduce cholesterol levels and triglycerides in the blood, often prescribed for patients with metabolic disorders."}{"title": "OMEPRAZOL:Omeprazol is a medication that the patient is taking to reduce the production of acid in the stomach. It is commonly used to treat gastroesophageal reflux disease and other related conditions."}{"title": "SUPLEMENTOS VITAM\u00cdNICOS:Vitamin supplements are dietary supplements that provide vitamins, often used to address deficiencies in patients with specific health conditions."}{"title": "BARIATRIC SURGERY:"}{"title": "NEUROPAT\u00cdA \u00d3PTICA BILATERAL:La neuropat\u00eda \u00f3ptica bilateral es un diagn\u00f3stico que se presenta a los 10-12 a\u00f1os, caracterizado por la disminuci\u00f3n progresiva de la agudeza visual y la atrofia \u00f3ptica observada en el fondo de ojo."}{"title": "POLINEUROPAT\u00cdA SENSITIVO MOTORA AXONAL:La polineuropat\u00eda sensitivo motora axonal es un diagn\u00f3stico que se presenta a los 16 a\u00f1os, caracterizado por debilidad progresiva en miembros y amiotrofia distal."}{"title": "HIPOACUSIA PROFUNDA BILATERAL:La hipoacusia profunda bilateral neurosensorial es un diagn\u00f3stico que se presenta a los 30 a\u00f1os, que requiere la colocaci\u00f3n de un implante coclear debido a la severidad de la p\u00e9rdida auditiva."}{"title": "LEUCOENCEFALOPAT\u00cdA SUPRATENTORIAL:La leucoencefalopat\u00eda supratentorial periventricular difusa es un hallazgo observado en la resonancia magn\u00e9tica nuclear cerebral, indicando cambios en la sustancia blanca del cerebro."}{"title": "S\u00cdNTOMAS DIGESTIVOS:Los s\u00edntomas digestivos incluyen p\u00e9rdida de peso, deposiciones blandas y episodios diarreicos, que se presentan en el paciente a lo largo del tiempo."}{"title": "AN\u00c1LISIS DE SANGRE:The entity \"AN\u00c1LISIS DE SANGRE\" refers to blood tests conducted on patients to assess various health indicators. These tests are essential for monitoring glucose levels, renal function, and other critical health parameters. The blood analysis reveals several important metrics, including blood sugar (glucemia), cholesterol levels, and vitamin concentrations, all of which are relevant for diagnosing the patient's health status. Overall, blood tests serve as a vital tool in evaluating the patient's overall health and nutritional parameters."}{"title": "ENDOSCOPIA:La endoscopia revela mucosa con atrofia parcheada y linfangiectasias, lo que contribuye al diagn\u00f3stico del paciente."}{"title": "C\u00c1PSULA ENDOSC\u00d3PICA:La c\u00e1psula endosc\u00f3pica visualiza linfangiectasias y edema en el yeyuno proximal, proporcionando informaci\u00f3n adicional sobre la condici\u00f3n del paciente."}{"title": "ATROFIA \u00d3PTICA:La atrofia \u00f3ptica es un hallazgo observado en el fondo de ojo del paciente, indicando da\u00f1o severo en la v\u00eda visual."}{"title": "DEBILIDAD PROGRESIVA:La debilidad progresiva es un s\u00edntoma que se presenta a los 16 a\u00f1os, afectando principalmente a los miembros inferiores y superiores."}{"title": "HIPOGLICEMIAS:Las hipoglucemias son episodios que ocurren debido a la suspensi\u00f3n irregular del tratamiento antidiab\u00e9tico, afectando la salud del paciente."}{"title": "SENSACI\u00d3N DE PLENITUD POSTPRANDIAL:La sensaci\u00f3n de plenitud postprandial es un s\u00edntoma que el paciente experimenta despu\u00e9s de las comidas, indicando problemas digestivos."}{"title": "IMAGEN DE RMN:La imagen de resonancia magn\u00e9tica nuclear (RMN) muestra cambios en la sustancia blanca del cerebro, lo que es relevante para el diagn\u00f3stico del paciente."}{"title": "MUCOSA INTESTINAL:La mucosa intestinal presenta atrofia y linfangiectasias, lo que se observa durante la endoscopia y es relevante para el diagn\u00f3stico del paciente."}{"title": "PATOLOG\u00cdAS:"}{"title": "TYMP:The TYMP gene is located on chromosome 22q13.33 and encodes a protein involved in the phosphorylation of thymidine, mutations in which cause MNGIE."}{"title": "GARONE:Garone is a researcher who reviewed 102 cases of MNGIE between 1988 and 2011, contributing to the understanding of the syndrome."}{"title": "TIMIDINA:Thymidine is a nucleoside that accumulates in patients with MNGIE due to the deficiency of thymidine phosphorylase."}{"title": "DEOXIURIDINA:Deoxyuridine is another nucleoside that accumulates in patients with MNGIE, indicating a metabolic disturbance."}{"title": "ALHAMIA PRISON:Alhamia Prison is a facility mentioned in the context of MNGIE, although not directly related to the syndrome itself."}{"title": "NEUROLOGICAL SYMPTOMS:Neurological symptoms associated with MNGIE include peripheral neuropathy, ptosis, ophthalmoplegia, and leukoencephalopathy."}{"title": "DIGESTIVE SYMPTOMS:Digestive symptoms of MNGIE include gastrointestinal dysmotility, early satiety, nausea, vomiting, and abdominal pain."}{"title": "CAQUEXIA:CAQUEXIA is a significant medical condition characterized by involuntary weight loss and muscle mass loss. It is particularly prevalent in patients suffering from Mitochondrial Neurogastrointestinal Encephalomyopathy (MNGIE), where it arises due to severe digestive symptoms. Additionally, cachexia is commonly observed in patients with advanced cancer, notably in those with adenocarcinoma of the pancreas. This condition not only contributes to malnutrition but also poses a considerable risk for further nutritional deficiencies. Overall, cachexia is a critical factor influencing the prognosis of affected individuals, especially in the context of cancer-related illnesses."}{"title": "ANALYTICAL FINDINGS:Analytical findings in MNGIE include elevated levels of thymidine and deoxyuridine in plasma, which are characteristic of the disorder."}{"title": "NEUROIMAGING FINDINGS:Neuroimaging findings in MNGIE typically show diffuse alterations in white matter, indicative of leukoencephalopathy."}{"title": "GENETIC SEQUENCING:Genetic sequencing is performed to identify mutations in the TYMP gene, confirming the diagnosis of MNGIE."}{"title": "CHROMOSOME 22Q13.33:"}{"title": "COENZYME Q 10:Coenzyme Q 10 is an antioxidant and a vital component of the mitochondrial respiratory chain, evaluated for its effects in mitochondrial diseases."}{"title": "CREATINE:Creatine is a substance that has been studied for its potential benefits in improving muscle strength in patients with mitochondrial diseases."}{"title": "THYMIDINE PHOSPHORYLASE:Thymidine phosphorylase is an enzyme whose activity is crucial for the metabolism of thymidine, and its deficiency is linked to MNGIE."}{"title": "HEMATOPOIETIC STEM CELL TRANSPLANT:Hematopoietic stem cell transplant is a treatment option being explored to correct the enzymatic deficiency in MNGIE."}{"title": "DIETARY ANTIOXIDANTS:Dietary antioxidants, including idebenone and vitamin E, have been studied for their potential clinical benefits in mitochondrial diseases."}{"title": "ENFERMEDAD CEL\u00cdACA:Enfermedad cel\u00edaca is an autoimmune disorder that affects the gastrointestinal tract and is included in the differential diagnosis of mitochondrial diseases."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME DE COLON IRRITABLE:S\u00edndrome de colon irritable is a gastrointestinal disorder that must be differentiated from mitochondrial diseases."}{"title": "DISTROFIA MUSCULAR CONG\u00c9NITA:Distrofia muscular cong\u00e9nita por d\u00e9ficit de merosina is a genetic disorder that affects muscle function and is relevant in the differential diagnosis of mitochondrial diseases."}{"title": "LEUCODISTROFIAS:Leucodistrofias are a group of disorders affecting the white matter of the brain, included in the differential diagnosis of mitochondrial diseases."}{"title": "ENFERMEDAD DE KRABBE:Enfermedad de Krabbe is a type of leukodystrophy that must be differentiated from mitochondrial diseases."}{"title": "ADRENOLEUCODISTROFIA:Adrenoleucodistrofia is a genetic disorder affecting the adrenal glands and white matter of the brain, relevant in the differential diagnosis of mitochondrial diseases."}{"title": "ENFERMEDAD DE CANAVAN:Enfermedad de Canavan is a genetic disorder that affects the brain and is included in the differential diagnosis of mitochondrial diseases."}{"title": "ENFERMEDAD DE ALEXANDER:Enfermedad de Alexander is a type of leukodystrophy that must be differentiated from mitochondrial diseases."}{"title": "LEUCOENCEFALOPAT\u00cdA CON SUSTANCIA BLANCA EVANESCENTE:Leucoencefalopat\u00eda con sustancia blanca evanescente is a disorder affecting the brain's white matter, relevant in the differential diagnosis of mitochondrial diseases."}{"title": "POLINEUROPAT\u00cdA DESMIELINIZANTE INFLAMATORIA CR\u00d3NICA:"}{"title": "TIMIDIN FOSFORILASA:Thymidine phosphorylase is an enzyme whose activity is crucial for correcting metabolic damage in patients with MNGIE."}{"title": "HEPATITIS:Hepatic transplantation is considered a viable treatment option for MNGIE patients due to the liver's role in producing thymidine phosphorylase."}{"title": "DIABETES MITOCONDRIAL:Mitochondrial diabetes is a condition that complicates treatment in patients with MNGIE, requiring careful management of blood sugar levels."}{"title": "COENZIMA Q 10:Coenzyme Q10 is a supplement used in the treatment of mitochondrial disorders, including MNGIE, to support cellular energy production."}{"title": "L-CARNITINA:L-Carnitine is a supplement that may be beneficial in managing symptoms for patients with mitochondrial diseases, such as MNGIE. Additionally, it has the potential to increase body weight and enhance the quality of life for cancer patients."}{"title": "ANTIDIAB\u00c9TICOS ORALES:Oral antidiabetic medications are prescribed to manage the patient's diabetes, which is complicated by mitochondrial dysfunction."}{"title": "SITAGLIPTINA:Sitagliptin is an oral antidiabetic medication utilized in the treatment regimen for patients with MNGIE (Mitochondrial Neurogastrointestinal Encephalomyopathy) as well as for controlling blood sugar levels in individuals with type 2 diabetes. This medication helps manage blood glucose levels effectively, making it a valuable option for patients requiring diabetes management."}¡1␀␀␀␀␀È1␀␀␀␀␀*1␀␀␀␀␀®1␀␀␀␀␀Ø1␀␀␀␀␀¨1␀␀␀␀␀ì1␀␀␀␀␀†1␀␀␀␀␀Ç1␀␀␀␀␀e1␀␀␀␀␀: 1␀␀␀␀␀!1␀␀␀␀␀"1␀␀␀␀␀‰"1␀␀␀␀␀M$1␀␀␀␀␀«%1␀␀␀␀␀A'1␀␀␀␀␀Q)1␀␀␀␀␀+1␀␀␀␀␀{-1␀␀␀␀␀ê/1␀␀␀␀␀Ú01␀␀␀␀␀H21␀␀␀␀␀ù31␀␀␀␀␀Z61␀␀␀␀␀∆71␀␀␀␀␀W91␀␀␀␀␀ß:1␀␀␀␀␀K=1␀␀␀␀␀Õ>1␀␀␀␀␀
